{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed","id":921517,"title":"What do you want from Warstriders in 3ed?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-26T09:14:48-07:00","id":921517,"title":"What do you want from Warstriders in 3ed?","content":"As the title suggests I thought that it would be interesting to discuss what we want (and dont want) for Warstriders this edition both from a mechanic and a setting point of view. I notice its comes up every now and then but lacks a dedicated thread.<br /> <br /> To get the ball rolling I would really like to feel that not all of the unique features of a given warstrider are locked behind the Evocation gate as I am very fond of diversity in design and appearance (a skeletal warstrider should not be anywhere near as hard to move as a heavily armoured warstrider nor as tough). Settings wise I would like to see some examples of Dynastic warstriders and the general modus operandi regarding how they are assigned and maintained by various faction (is it inherited or assignment based?).<br /> <br /> What does everyone else hope/dread regarding Warstriders?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T09:27:03-07:00","id":921524,"title":"","content":"My pipe dream? <br /> <br /> I want two rule options for war striders. One where they are considered armor and rare. This would be for games with only one war strider. The other where they are consider a vehicle and you can have full out battles between war striders and behemoths. This would be for the more Pacific Rim type games. The second option may be more suitable for a Shard setting, but that's why it's a pipe dream. <br /> <br /> More seriously, I want war striders and thier wearers/pilots to have a strong connection. I rather not get into AI/Jarvis territory, but more like a captain and his ship. The pilot knows the war strider and has discovered evocations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T09:46:00-07:00","id":921525,"title":"","content":"I'd like warstriders to require specific conditions to even activate, like having a specific principal, blood line, ability or attribute combinations, representing the things that are important to the strider in its pilot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T10:01:41-07:00","id":921535,"title":"","content":"I'd like them to be actually usable in regular gameplay. Not just Artifact N/A, on grounds of 'you can have one if your ST feels like it', not this labarynthine subsystem like Craft that's too intimidating for me or my friends to tackle. Not just a table of evocations that will make them awesome someday if I sink enough Solar XP on them. If we get Warstrider rules that I can use in a game and enjoy, I will be happy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T10:06:04-07:00","id":921537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=921524#post921524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More seriously, I want war striders and thier wearers/pilots to have a strong connection. I rather not get into AI/Jarvis territory, but more like a captain and his ship. The pilot knows the war strider and has discovered evocations.</div> </div> </div> </div>This exactly. This is the foundation of artifacts in Ex3 and I think Warstriders have a wonderful opportunity to embody these features the strongest.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think it might be neat to have each Warstrider has something of a purpose. Not in the same sense as a Martial Art style, but in the sense of like a Defining Intimacy. The thing can do whatever you need it to do, but when it's doing its designed purpose (or following its Defining Intimacy) it gains a bonus or....... actually I just realized this is exactly what Evocations are meant to represent, so I guess it's just back to my first point. If you're using it the way it wants to be used, then you can use its evocations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T10:17:18-07:00","id":921542,"title":"","content":"Robotech/Macross...there I said it.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/aMpgLjryyHo\" data-code=\"aMpgLjryyHo\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/aMpgLjryyHo/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T10:18:50-07:00","id":921543,"title":"","content":"I was thinking that warstriders would not be overwhelming combatants against exalted level opponents. Rather, though I don't know how to model this, they would be something like an MA+Artifact with evocations combo that would grant the users a sort of focused, offensive capability while was very useful for the sorts of things the 'strider was meant to do.<br /> <br /> For example, if the 'strider was crafted to fight behemoths an E5 dawn would probably do that just as well or better and climbing in one would not significantly improve the Dawn's ability in that situation. But a Twilight or Eclipse, who don't have the Dawn's combat suite, would gain a massive increase in their ability to contribute. (to say nothing of a mortal). A fight between the Dawn without a 'strider and one of her circlemates with one would be FAR closer than a fight where neither had one and the outcome might actually be in question.<br /> <br /> I would also like it if those that bond with them are better than those who just fall into the cockpit, perhaps represented by unlocking evocation, many of which might be permanent charm equivalents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T10:25:00-07:00","id":921550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=921543#post921543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking that warstriders would not be overwhelming combatants against exalted level opponents. Rather, though I don't know how to model this, they would be something like an MA+Artifact with evocations combo that would grant the users a sort of focused, offensive capability while was very useful for the sorts of things the 'strider was meant to do.<br /> <br /> For example, if the 'strider was crafted to fight behemoths an E5 dawn would probably do that just as well or better and climbing in one would not significantly improve the Dawn's ability in that situation. But a Twilight or Eclipse, who don't have the Dawn's combat suite, would gain a massive increase in their ability to contribute. (to say nothing of a mortal). A fight between the Dawn without a 'strider and one of her circlemates with one would be FAR closer than a fight where neither had one and the outcome might actually be in question.<br /> <br /> I would also like it if those that bond with them are better than those who just fall into the cockpit, perhaps represented by unlocking evocation, many of which might be permanent charm equivalents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the problem that I see with that is that an artifact is typically meant to be a tool to enhance power rather than just something with a fixed tier of power, in previous editions the main selling points of striders was that you could still effectively use all your charms while wearing them so that Dawn would retain all of their might while gaining the bonus of wearing a giant suit of mega-death.<br /> <br /> Personally though, the idea of a legendary warmachine that is useless to the living siege engines of the Celestial host leaves a bad taste in my mouth. I prefer to think that while a non=Dawn would rival a Dawn that a Dawn wearing a warstrider would have a considerable advantage against a Dawn without one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T10:57:22-07:00","id":921564,"title":"","content":"Big enough to be pivotal to a character concept but not so big that it twists any game you put one in into a mecha anime. My pipe dream is for compelling upkeep and repair, 2e shoved it off-screen so it felt like a car servicing rather than owning a car after the apocalypse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T11:07:19-07:00","id":921571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=921564#post921564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Big enough to be pivotal to a character concept but not so big that it twists any game you put one in into a mecha anime. My pipe dream is for compelling upkeep and repair, 2e shoved it off-screen so it felt like a car servicing rather than owning a car after the apocalypse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I almost hope for a feel like the Imperial Knight lore from 40k where it feels like a great honor to be chosen, my strider can't just be passed around, and while being awe inspiring it doesn't make me utterly invincible, and a dawn of equal skill and potential without it can still win by being clever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T11:12:52-07:00","id":921573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=921571#post921571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I almost hope for a feel like the Imperial Knight lore from 40k where it feels like a great honor to be chosen, my strider can't just be passed around, and while being awe inspiring it doesn't make me utterly invincible, and a dawn of equal skill and potential without it can still win by being clever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would also like for the prestige of owning one to be almost as useful as the strider itself, you dont even need it working for the threat of it to be priceless when threatening a foe. Daiklaves and all are not quite as visible a threat (cant expect people to be versed on Evocations) and no one has a proper scale of how dangerous a 'Celestial' exalt can be, but a giant doom-golem made of materials of incalculable wealth? That is a very clear and visceral threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T11:27:58-07:00","id":921582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=921573#post921573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also like for the prestige of owning one to be almost as useful as the strider itself, you dont even need it working for the threat of it to be priceless when threatening a foe. Daiklaves and all are not quite as visible a threat (cant expect people to be versed on Evocations) and no one has a proper scale of how dangerous a 'Celestial' exalt can be, but a giant doom-golem made of materials of incalculable wealth? That is a very clear and visceral threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, exactly! Plus when I go to take my Father's place as the operator there should be ceremony, fanfare, a house celebration, it should feel like an important day. Like so big the head of the house herself shows up to anoit my head before the bond between me and the colossal war god is formed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 06-26-2016, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T11:42:00-07:00","id":921595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eltacolibre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=921542#post921542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Robotech/Macross...there I said it.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/aMpgLjryyHo\" data-code=\"aMpgLjryyHo\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/aMpgLjryyHo/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Valkyries are a great deal too far on the &quot;real&quot; robot side. Warstriders are supposed to be firmly within the &quot;super&quot; robot type, like Mazinger with magic. I mean, one might change into a flying dragon-like thing in a manner of a giant warbird, but it'd be like with Escaflowne.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T12:15:02-07:00","id":921611,"title":"","content":"I want Warstriders that change and alter to their riders, not super specialized things. I want a Warstrider that has a very strong pilot in it to be stronger physically than the same warstrider if it's bonded to a very smart person. I want the rider to shape the ride - I want them to embrace the old evocation rules, where the idea was that every single wielder of any weapon will have different evocations, because the evocations are equal parts the weapon's story <i>and</i> the bond the person has with it. I want these to be <i>magical</i> things, that change and alter not based on hard science and upgrades or changing weapons, but based on the mentality of their riders. I don't want a warstrider pilot to go 'ah, I need to switch to long range, so let me go change my arm to a long reach arm', I want a brawl warstrider pilot to go 'we need long range support, hey ARchery Dude, switch out with me and pilot for a bit', and have the warstrider alter to what its rider is.<br /> <br /> I want magical super armor giants, not robots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T12:45:02-07:00","id":921635,"title":"","content":"I want warstriders to have the kind of power that makes them distinct from a powerful daiklave or something (not just in scope, but in form) and makes them seem valuable and tactically relevant. In other words, I want them to be more than just some boosted physical stats and a selection of minor generic bonuses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T12:46:02-07:00","id":921637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=921550#post921550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the problem that I see with that is that an artifact is typically meant to be a tool to enhance power rather than just something with a fixed tier of power, in previous editions the main selling points of striders was that you could still effectively use all your charms while wearing them so that Dawn would retain all of their might while gaining the bonus of wearing a giant suit of mega-death.<br /> <br /> Personally though, the idea of a legendary warmachine that is useless to the living siege engines of the Celestial host leaves a bad taste in my mouth. I prefer to think that while a non=Dawn would rival a Dawn that a Dawn wearing a warstrider would have a considerable advantage against a Dawn without one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking of it more as a supplemental ability charmset. Dawn + 'strider would have that extra well of charms to draw from compared to Dawn sans 'strider which would grant more options, many quite powerful, but wouldn't make it a sure victory. Sort of like how a Dawn can already slay armies but a Dawn with White Reaper can do it more efficiently.<br /> <br /> That is why I made the MA comparison. The Dawns, who are already good at fighting, have less to gain than those who are not already good at fighting, but would still have a higher total level of power than those without. Relative advantage sort of deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T13:35:43-07:00","id":921664,"title":"","content":"What I want?<br /> <br /> I wanna feel that power surge <br /> Two minds that were made to merge <br /> Don\u2019t make me miss the rush <br /> Take me to the crush <br /> <br /> I wanna hear that roarin sound <br /> When I walk I will shake the ground<br /> Don\u2019t make me miss the rush <br /> Take me to the crush","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1521-jang","name":"Jang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1521_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T13:42:59-07:00","id":921666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=921664#post921664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I want?<br /> <br /> I wanna feel that power surge<br /> Two minds that were made to merge<br /> Don\u2019t make me miss the rush<br /> Take me to the crush<br /> <br /> I wanna hear that roarin sound<br /> When I walk I will shake the ground<br /> Don\u2019t make me miss the rush<br /> Take me to the crush</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay, while my base desires for Warstriders is pretty much just &quot;More Escaflowne, plz&quot;, I gotta admit, a solid framework that, even if something like a Jaeger is too gonzo for settings as written, it's easy enough to modify and upscale to reach that level of insanity would be awesome.<br /> #GipsyDanger4Life","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T17:57:48-07:00","id":921779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=921582#post921582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, exactly! Plus when I go to take my Father's place as the operator there should be ceremony, fanfare, a house celebration, it should feel like an important day. Like so big the head of the house herself shows up to anoit my head before the bond between me and the colossal war god is formed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have this scene in my head where a Veteran of Thorns rises from her hospital bed and limps over to the remains of her totalled war strider. She falls to her knees in tears and apologizes to the war strider for failing it. <br /> <br /> I want that type of emotional relationship with a war strider. I want most pilots to have an intimacy with thier war strider. A character that treats it as a peice of machinery will not get as much power and ability out of the artifact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T18:00:52-07:00","id":921780,"title":"","content":"BEAST MODE","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T18:48:54-07:00","id":921804,"title":"","content":"I said this in another thread...<br /> <br /> The new Voltron.<br /> <br /> No, I mean it. If you haven't yet, watch the first (admittedly triple-length) first episode of Voltron: Legendary Defender. The new studio does a LOT to make the Lions feel like more than just machines.<br /> <br /> Each Lion will only be piloted by people that fit certain criteria. Like the Green Lion only accepts inquisitive thinker-types, the Yellow accepts loyal friends that put others above themselves, the Black Lion accepts born leaders.<br /> <br /> The Lions aren't like, fully self-aware, like full-on talking AI. Not that we've seen yet, anyway. But they DO help coax their pilots, help them move, and will like, deploy certain things in response to their pilot's needs, to help them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 06-26-2016, 09:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T19:35:19-07:00","id":921819,"title":"","content":"OK *rubs together hands*<ul><li>Evocations</li> <li>A way to slot them into a variety of scenarios without those scenarios becoming decidedly imbalanced in favor of the side with Warstriders.</li> <li>A way for contemporary Craft-focused characters to build them. Not necessarily mass produce them, or build them easily, but a way</li> <li>Don't tie their construction to singular Magical Materials; to wit, the building process should be similar to building a Manse rather than forging an Artifact</li> <li>The Legendary Size Merit should be hard coded into Warstrider rules</li> <li>Less parity in the availability of Warstriders, e.g.: certain factions and Exalts generally have no business piloting Warstriders (Lunars, Liminals, Infernals, Exigents, Sidereals), due either to a reasonable lack of necessary infrastructure (Liminals, Exigents) or access to comparable, but fundamentally different magics (Lunars, Inferals, Sidereals), not to say that they couldn't, given access, but what's available isn't designed for them, in so far as most of the readily (relative term) available Warstriders are going to be First Age relics or Shogunate/Realm attempts to duplicate those relics.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 06-26-2016, 10:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T20:05:08-07:00","id":921825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=921819#post921819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK *rubs together hands*<br /> A way to slot them into a variety of scenarios without those scenarios becoming decidedly imbalanced in favor of the side with Warstriders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted OGRE could be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T21:57:32-07:00","id":921850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=921595#post921595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Valkyries are a great deal too far on the &quot;real&quot; robot side. Warstriders are supposed to be firmly within the &quot;super&quot; robot type, like Mazinger with magic. I mean, one might change into a flying dragon-like thing in a manner of a giant warbird, but it'd be like with Escaflowne.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I asked the developers if we would be able to cludge something like &quot;Warwalkers&quot; together.<br /> <br /> Basically, the melefs to the guymelefs. The mobile suits to the gundams.<br /> <br /> Mook mecha for mecha-centric games.<br /> <br /> <br /> But I can't imagine the point of including a warstrider in a game at all without it becoming the focus of the game. Either everyone who wants to fight is using a warstrider, or the singular warstrider is the macguffin that drives the plot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T23:28:06-07:00","id":921868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=921825#post921825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exalted OGRE could be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>True enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T01:24:40-07:00","id":921893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=921804#post921804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said this in another thread...<br /> <br /> The new Voltron.<br /> <br /> No, I mean it. If you haven't yet, watch the first (admittedly triple-length) first episode of Voltron: Legendary Defender. The new studio does a LOT to make the Lions feel like more than just machines.<br /> <br /> Each Lion will only be piloted by people that fit certain criteria. Like the Green Lion only accepts inquisitive thinker-types, the Yellow accepts loyal friends that put others above themselves, the Black Lion accepts born leaders.<br /> <br /> The Lions aren't like, fully self-aware, like full-on talking AI. Not that we've seen yet, anyway. But they DO help coax their pilots, help them move, and will like, deploy certain things in response to their pilot's needs, to help them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I came here to say this same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T04:51:17-07:00","id":921937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=921819#post921819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK *rubs together hands*<br /> certain factions and Exalts generally have no business piloting Warstriders (Lunars, Liminals, Infernals, Exigents, Sidereals), due either to a reasonable lack of necessary infrastructure (Liminals, Exigents) or access to comparable, but fundamentally different magics (Lunars, Inferals, Sidereals), not to say that they couldn't, given access,</div> </div> </div> </div>Hellstriders are one of the coolest things in 2E, so I hope 3E has something with a similar aesthetic, even if it's no longer made of demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T05:51:54-07:00","id":921947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=921564#post921564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Big enough to be pivotal to a character concept but not so big that it twists any game you put one in into a mecha anime. My pipe dream is for compelling upkeep and repair, 2e shoved it off-screen so it felt like a car servicing rather than owning a car after the apocalypse.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. I want my group's Craft supernal Twilight to make one and use it to awesome effect, but I don't want him to make one for everyone else in the game (especially not the Dawn).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9749-andrew-d","name":"Andrew D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T06:24:23-07:00","id":921966,"title":"","content":"I want Warstriders to have mechanics that justify their narrative place in Ex3. Including:<br /> <br /> The Realm and Lookshy has them, and can use them, but does it only in dire circumstances.<br /> They can actually do the things they are said to do (destroy armies).<br /> Have maintenance requirements that are meaningful, instead of just checking boxes.<br /> <br /> And for all that, I also want them to be accessible to PCs. One of the justifications for pulling back 'striders in this edition is the idea that by doing so PCs owning one would be more significant. The mechanics need to accomplish all the points above and yet it's still plausible for PCs to own and maintain one, or even one for each PC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T08:14:15-07:00","id":922016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=921850#post921850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why I asked the developers if we would be able to cludge something like &quot;Warwalkers&quot; together.<br /> <br /> Basically, the melefs to the guymelefs. The mobile suits to the gundams.<br /> <br /> Mook mecha for mecha-centric games.<br /> <br /> <br /> But I can't imagine the point of including a warstrider in a game at all without it becoming the focus of the game. Either everyone who wants to fight is using a warstrider, or the singular warstrider is the macguffin that drives the plot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't they mention using the automaton/walking statue stats for disposable mecha?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T09:44:05-07:00","id":922055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=921966#post921966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want Warstriders to have mechanics that justify their narrative place in Ex3. Including:<br /> <br /> The Realm and Lookshy has them, and can use them, but does it only in dire circumstances.<br /> They can actually do the things they are said to do (destroy armies).<br /> Have maintenance requirements that are meaningful, instead of just checking boxes.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI believe this is a better way of saying what I was trying to say before.<br /> <br /> On the subject of it being plausible to have one, I wonder at a point that it might be easier to kill the person inside than destroying the warstrider itself, and that approaching such a warstrider afterwards becomes inadvisable, so it just gets left there until a hill forms over it.<br /> <br /> Hmm, that last part deviated into a specific idea rather than a general point, but you take my meaning.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T09:56:59-07:00","id":922062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=922055#post922055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI believe this is a better way of saying what I was trying to say before.<br /> <br /> On the subject of it being plausible to have one, I wonder at a point that it might be easier to kill the person inside than destroying the warstrider itself, and that approaching such a warstrider afterwards becomes inadvisable, so it just gets left there until a hill forms over it.<br /> <br /> Hmm, that last part deviated into a specific idea rather than a general point, but you take my meaning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the nature of artifacts in this edition I would hazard to say that damaging or even rendering them useless is certainly plausible (for Exalted anyway) but truly destroying them is absurdly difficult at best (also depending on the artifact there is a very good chance of it somehow killing you if you manage to anger it).<br /> Killing a pilot? Difficult but possible, destroying the ancient god-golem? Good luck with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T10:21:45-07:00","id":922072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=921937#post921937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hellstriders are one of the coolest things in 2E, so I hope 3E has something with a similar aesthetic, even if it's no longer made of demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Existing, of course, but it should be stressed that they are exceptional in the extreme, and relatively new tech for Hell's Chosen, whereas the alternative I'd want, being able to summon or become Behemoths, should be more SOP for GSPs trying to lay siege or put down armed resistance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T11:48:09-07:00","id":922127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=922016#post922016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Didn't they mention using the automaton/walking statue stats for disposable mecha?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they did. So, we should be covered.<br /> <br /> Hopefully. It depends on whether they considered the possibility of an Exalt being stuck with only a Leo because his Gundam Wing is flying toward the sun. They might have only been thinking of mortal NPCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 06-27-2016, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T14:32:25-07:00","id":922220,"title":"","content":"I want to feel like a badass when I'm in a warstrider. I also want to be able to fight outside of a warstrider, or even against warstriders, without feeling like a chump. I'm willing to give a little on the second part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T16:01:16-07:00","id":922255,"title":"","content":"I would like warstriders to be very cool, but very expensive. Not only in motes/evocations, but in support and maintenance costs. Like, a warstrider burns 1 Gold Xp per turn of combat. This way, the Warstrider can be very much worth it when used wisely, but not a fix-all and replacement for everything else. Also, it makes useful to get a sense that 'it takes a village' to make a warstrider work. The Dawn who rides it dependes on the twilight who will keep it running, depends on the eclipse to get the materials, the night to steal them, the Zenith to comandeer them, and so on. It also makes it so that the pilot cannot be on the armor all the time, and has a reason to fight on his own.<br /> <br /> Even then evocations could make it so that the maintenance costs are mitigated or outright removed, for a large investiment, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T16:16:16-07:00","id":922267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=921937#post921937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hellstriders are one of the coolest things in 2E, so I hope 3E has something with a similar aesthetic, even if it's no longer made of demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I understand it correctly you can totally still make a warstrider out of demons (or the bones of mystical creatures like behemoths), it just no longer has a different name making it sound like it is an entirely different thing that functions exactly like a warstrider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T16:22:50-07:00","id":922273,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure the capacity to go berserk Evangellion-style is &quot;exactly&quot; like a warstrider, but yeah, under the new paradigm it could well be made at least partially out of demonic materials and have a mind of it's own, so I think we're good on that front.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T16:57:13-07:00","id":922297,"title":"","content":"Double post","signature":"","edited":{"userid":779,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","user":"NuSoardGraphite","date":". 06-27-2016, 08:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T17:02:52-07:00","id":922298,"title":"","content":"I want warstriders to feel and play like this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/YK38WzlNvfk\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/YK38WzlNvfk\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/YK38WzlNvfk\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/YK38WzlNvfk </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T17:53:50-07:00","id":922321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=922298#post922298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want warstriders to feel and play like this:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/YK38WzlNvfk\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/YK38WzlNvfk</a></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHmm, I need to go back and re-watch Escaflowne some time, and continue it to the end; I had forgotten how thrilling it is.<br /> <br /> Thinking more on it, I think Totentanz expressed the right point about warstriders having powers that warrant having them, but I still think what those actual powers are is the mouse that is not given much thought to tying the bell on the cat.<br /> <br /> I think warstriders exist in an odd space in Exalted, in that they're things that emulate genre fiction of giant robots or magic armour or what have you, but that fiction tends not to attribute superhuman powers to the actual pilot (excepting things that actually aid the piloting such as improved reflexes or some kind of prescience). Part of the issue with the Exalted is that they can already be mighty in a manner that most inspirational fiction requires you to don the suit to be able to get at. That's why I think that the prior generic warstrider enhancement of greater strength doesn't cut it; it would be like giving Superman a giant mech.<br /> <br /> At the same time, while I want its powers to have something more, I think them varying too wildly makes the actual aesthetic of the warstrider itself feel irrelevant and perfunctory; you've got a set of generic weapons and powers hanging off of a platform that incidentally resembles a human. It's similar to issues I've had with manses, and even some Artifacts.<br /> <br /> So I'm trying to think of what would really make the warstrider; what its image would be, so that one could devise powers that would be evocative of that image.<br /> <br /> For the moment, I'm thinking of something like the warstrider as being a bit like a monument, in terms of the oversized image of a human as something to inspire awe. The warstrider as a massive icon of authority, of martial valour, the icon of a god of war striding majestically across the battlefield. It's not just a collection of weapons hanging off of a large suit of armour that an Exalt must command from the inside, it is the Exalted writing themselves large. Within a single warstrider, you can get an image with more variety and nuance than the most specific characters of daiklaves and similar, so a red jade warstrider as a fiery icon of battle an Exalt can elevate themselves into would have more avenues of expression than something like Volcano Cutter's direct violent eruptions, so there's a measure of balance between them even if the warstrider is technically more powerful (and may have a heavier fiery apocalypse type of attack).<br /> <br /> Think Doctor Manhatten walking as a giant through the burning fields of Vietnam.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T18:05:51-07:00","id":922326,"title":"","content":"I had an idea of a cliff hanger in one of my Quest's Shogunate Manga where a Solar Anathema inflicted some major damage on a war strider. With just his sword.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T19:21:59-07:00","id":922365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=922298#post922298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want warstriders to feel and play like this:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/YK38WzlNvfk\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/YK38WzlNvfk</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Complete with Dance of Curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T20:39:20-07:00","id":922419,"title":"","content":"One thing I do not want is the return of maintenance cost. Much better, I think, to treat damage to Warstriders as what it is: damage to a First Age Artifact, which is covered in the Artifact rules for Crafting in a way that involves the PCs in a way that just assessing a Resources cost doesn't and can't. I created a character whom I could justify having the ability to do maintenance on one. &quot;I can fix this. Give me a few months to build a shop and make the tools. What? I'm a smith, I'm a sorceress, I grew up in a First Age crafters' manse. We'll need heavy block-and-tackle, a set of Hyperion keys, a water powered prayer organ, and a sunlight graver. Also a new gasket for the knee joint. That one's going to be tricky.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 06-27-2016, 11:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T22:32:58-07:00","id":922467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=922298#post922298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want warstriders to feel and play like this:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/YK38WzlNvfk\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/YK38WzlNvfk</a></div> </div> </div> </div>This. Totally.<br /> <br /> Also, the old guy with the big sword? That is how Dawn Castes and Lunar Exalted should fight Warstriders. That guy is awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11910-wick-black","name":"Wick Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T22:39:14-07:00","id":922469,"title":"","content":"Coming off playing a 2e Dragonblooded Modern game where we were basically power rangers, I would not be upset if wastriders had rules that let them combine. Sworn brotherhood as one etc etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T22:59:00-07:00","id":922472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wick Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=922467#post922467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This. Totally.<br /> <br /> Also, the old guy with the big sword? That is how Dawn Castes and Lunar Exalted should fight Warstriders. That guy is awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>My thoughts exactly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T09:00:05-07:00","id":922668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wick Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=922467#post922467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This. Totally.<br /> <br /> Also, the old guy with the big sword? That is how Dawn Castes and Lunar Exalted should fight Warstriders. That guy is awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a Classic Battletech player and one of the things I have loved back in the day was Elementals. Over to top warriors in powered armor who when they swarmed over your 100 ton mech, the would start ripping up the armor plating and eventually bring you down. They would be like ants tearing at it. Normal infantry guys died like nothing else. Elementals...these guys are what I think of when I think of a Exalted vs. A 'Strider. Will they take it down easy? Hell no. But they aren't hopelessly out classed. The circle might have to work together to do it too. The lone dawn is just going to slow it down, unless he gets smart, and thinks outside the box, otherwise a strider should give a lone dawn a very credible threat of being reduced to a red gooey paste. Is that going to happen, maybe 4 out of 10 times the dawn gets too cocky and ends up getting splattered on a 'Strider Daiklave, knocked out, crippled or failing to protect his target, in short they lose. Another 4 out of 10 times I figure he wins, within varying degrees of success. Such as driving off the enemy as opposed to outright victory. Maybe pushing the Strider to the limits of it's operational time, so the pilot opts to retreat or putting enough damage on the thing to make the pilot decide that winning this fight is too costly for their taste. Or yes managing to kill the pilot or &quot;break&quot; the strider. The remaining 2 out of 10 times the strider pilot fights the dawn to a stand still.<br /> <br /> Now that said I figure some things will shift these numbers around. Things like, the whole circle participating in the battle. The 'Strider pilot is a Dawn/Slayer/Dusk caste, weapons load out of the strider. Different levels of essence, does the Lone dawn have as their supernal their combat ability, or was it Resistance, or war?<br /> <br /> Now that said, honestly this thread caused me to start reading up on Imperial Knights, and I love how others brought up that you should have an intimacy to your strider. Plus since you bond to the machine with your soul it has fragments of the souls of every pilot and what they held dear floating around in it. So suddenly becoming a bit more like your Mom or Dad who used it before you, isn't so unlikely because now your bonded to those fragments of their souls. I just found this out but, apparently bonding to the Imperial Knight (if used as an example of a 'strider) causes you to develop that intimacy plus one to the duties and hierarchy of a knight. In in the terms of our setting the necrotic 'striders used by the underworld's forces that would be a Tie of Loyalty to a Deathlord. And a principal they approved of as well that you instantly gain and that cannot be weakened as long as you are bonded to your machine. Which I could see as something interesting in the way of Dynastic striders that suddenly the pilot feels a love like Fealty to the Empress, and has a defining principal of upholding the empire even when before they were considering bringing it down. I might like having that as a thing for 'striders in my setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T09:20:35-07:00","id":922678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=922469#post922469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coming off playing a 2e Dragonblooded Modern game where we were basically power rangers, I would not be upset if wastriders had rules that let them combine. Sworn brotherhood as one etc etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry to interrupt, but where is your avatar from?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T09:37:26-07:00","id":922685,"title":"","content":"The paradox that I cannot help but notice is people wanting for warstriders to be rare and require heavy maintenance while at the same time not be an overwhelming threat to an average Dawn and not be 'better' than any other given artifact.<br /> <br /> I personally think that it should a rare Dawn who can take down a warstrider single-handedly with the odds favouring the more well-armed and canny opponent. I also think that if a warstrider is going to require extensive upkeep then it needs something to give it an advantage over somethong like say Volcano Cutter which has no visible downsides to its mere existence. My main concern with this is that 'superiority' between two equally rated artifacts should come from who has the greatest rapport with their artifact not a generic matter of making it into either Shadow of the Collosus versus 'I need to finish this fight before this thing breaks again.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T09:52:36-07:00","id":922693,"title":"","content":"I want my warstriders to be apocalyptic engines, decidedly setting them as a large scale threat. A warstrider comes fight an exalt, you worry. A warstrider comes fight an army, or besiege a town, you shit bricks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T10:12:32-07:00","id":922706,"title":"","content":"Warstriders are stated to be N/A Artifacts, so they need to be mechanically amazing, with the stats of articulated plate, smashfists and god-kicking boots combined as the absolute minimum for the least of them, the ones operating on the &quot;power armour&quot; level. The ones you pilot rather than wear should have their own appropriately amazing stats. Strength in particular should be very high. Lots of soak and hardness. Evocations based around amplifying the pilot's Charms to operate on the warstrider level. High attunement costs and the mecha versions should require hearthstones as well. Basically, they should be amazing and wondrous things you only bring out in time of dire need, when the situation has crossed the Godzilla threshold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T11:30:38-07:00","id":922750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=922685#post922685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally think that it should a rare Dawn who can take down a warstrider single-handedly with the odds favouring the more well-armed and canny opponent. I also think that if a warstrider is going to require extensive upkeep then it needs something to give it an advantage over something like say Volcano Cutter which has no visible downsides to its mere existence. My main concern with this is that 'superiority' between two equally rated artifacts should come from who has the greatest rapport with their artifact not a generic matter of making it into either Shadow of the Collosus versus 'I need to finish this fight before this thing breaks again.'</div> </div> </div> </div>This is part of why I said that at a minimum, a Warstrider should grant the Legendary Size creature merit, as that places a difficult but not insurmountable obstacle to fighting one single-handedly. It would necessitate a balance of damage and stat-boosters against defensive and accuracy-boosting charms that, outside of choosing the right Supernals and mono-focusing on taking down legendarily sized foes, would monopolize a lot of a starting character's resources.<br /> On the other hand, I agree with LadyLens that the 3e Craft system is robust enough to handle the upkeep and building of Warstriders without bolting on an extraneous Maintenance system.<br /> Lastly, if they do nothing to tone down the impact of Warstrider warfare on the game, then they really should remain as N/A-level Artifacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T11:50:44-07:00","id":922758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=922685#post922685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The paradox that I cannot help but notice is people wanting for warstriders to be rare and require heavy maintenance while at the same time not be an overwhelming threat to an average Dawn and not be 'better' than any other given artifact.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think an average Dawn should be able to take out a Warstrider.<br /> <br /> An Essence 5 Dawn PC should be able to solo a Warstrider*. And that scene should be Epic.<br /> <br /> *What else should an Essence 5 Dawn be able to take on that is better than a War Strider? Behemoth? Another Dawn PC in a Warstrider? The Unconquered Sun himself?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 06-28-2016, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T12:09:38-07:00","id":922770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=922685#post922685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The paradox that I cannot help but notice is people wanting for warstriders to be rare and require heavy maintenance while at the same time not be an overwhelming threat to an average Dawn and not be 'better' than any other given artifact.<br /> <br /> I personally think that it should a rare Dawn who can take down a warstrider single-handedly with the odds favouring the more well-armed and canny opponent. I also think that if a warstrider is going to require extensive upkeep then it needs something to give it an advantage over somethong like say Volcano Cutter which has no visible downsides to its mere existence. My main concern with this is that 'superiority' between two equally rated artifacts should come from who has the greatest rapport with their artifact not a generic matter of making it into either Shadow of the Collosus versus 'I need to finish this fight before this thing breaks again.'</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it so so much of &quot;this thing will break&quot; as opposed to &quot;I have a half hour of combat time before this thing runs out of fuel&quot; in 2e terms I can picture it burning out the hearth stone for the next 4 hours rendering it inert, so I wonder what sort of limits we will see on 'striders and if they will have an operational time limit based on a resource that when it expires maybe the exalt has to give their own essence to power it every turn, creating a greater drain on their resources.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that is why I gave a Dawn caste a 4 in 10 chance of winning, including victory by preventing the 'strider pilot from completing his objective and instead of a decisive victory. I also did not indicate the degree of safety for the Dawn caste who I likely imagine will not be exiting the battle unarmed but rather likely with a broken or removed arm or shattered body needing months of care from the twilight healer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T12:29:45-07:00","id":922779,"title":"","content":"I sort of feel that there's precious little that can challenge a 5 Essence Celestial Exalt Circle already (and it's not a bigger Celestial or maybe a couple of Gods), and a big Warstrider seems a fit match for a circle like that, or maybe for a single E6-7 Celestial. <br /> Maybe some low-tech clunky Warstrider made out of mostly iron and mundane material could exist and be way easier to defeat. But if I try to imagine a 15-20m tall block of Jade (or worse), suddenly the odds of the overpowered little guy with the silly huge sword should be rather low. Especially if there's another Exalt inside. Or if the 'strider uses the Dawn's Daiklave bigger sister.<br /> <br /> But again, I feel that the progression of power in Exalted, at least in 2E ramps waaay to fast in the 5-6 Essence range (especially consider it's just halfway to the theoretical top).<br /> I hope that in 3E this is a bit more spread out and Warstrider's balance plays a part in that. I'd hate to see them to pushed down in power just to be accessible early.<br /> On the other hand I'd be perfectly fine in seeing smaller, clumsier and weaker 'striders at that range. <br /> <br /> I guess my ideal would be some kind of Gurrenn Lagann progression of power, from the silly small and cheap robot used to mine and repurposed to fight, to the big badass one you get to release against an army or a behemoth.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7835-bard","name":"Bard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T12:31:39-07:00","id":922782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=922779#post922779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But again, I feel that the progression of power in Exalted, at least in 2E ramps waaay to fast in the 5-6 Essence range (especially consider it's just halfway to the theoretical top).<br /> I hope that in 3E this is a bit more spread out and Warstrider's balance plays a part in that. I'd hate to see them to pushed down in power just to be accessible early.<br /> On the other hand I'd be perfectly fine in seeing smaller, clumsier and weaker 'striders at that range.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Base Warstrider may be weaker at Essence 1. As your character grows, you gain access to better Warstrider Evocations. Basically, your warstrider grows with you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T12:47:37-07:00","id":922791,"title":"","content":"I really need to get my hands on a 3E book :V There's way to much I don't know yet. <br /> Wouldn't that mean that you've got this huge cool mecha that needs to be powered down to be balanced with Essence 1 charms (with possibly an artifact added)? And end up being a fair fight with a random MA Celestial with Gloves of Punching+1? <br /> <br /> Talking without considering the rules for a second, I'd like for warstrider to be something BIG, that is hard to obtain and service (something that a single individual or small group can't achieve, even one made of Celestials), absolutely not something you get at creation or early in the game (except maybe as a final boss at around 3-4E) and something that you can't use in normal &quot;adventuring&quot;, but that when you eventually end up pulling out storage just makes a mess of things that you couldn't even consider fighting without it, at least without getting another 2-3 essence and some serious &quot;small&quot; artifacts. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7835-bard","name":"Bard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T12:51:16-07:00","id":922793,"title":"","content":"Evocations is an Ex3 Mechanic where your Artifact basically get its own charm set*. Like other charm sets, it has charms at various Essence Levels. <br /> <br /> So like your Artifact Sword, a War Strider has base stats. Then as you play your character, you can unlock Evocations that make your warstrider more powerful. It's less dumbing down your warstrider and more &quot;I discovered my War Strider does this awesome thing, yesterday! Here, hold me sake and watch this!&quot;<br /> <br /> *People who have more familiarity with Ex3 correct me if I am wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 06-28-2016, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T13:28:33-07:00","id":922817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=922793#post922793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*People who have more familiarity with Ex3 correct me if I am wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Charm set&quot; might be misleading, as there isn't an artifact yet that has more than five charms.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T13:29:49-07:00","id":922819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=922817#post922817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Charm set&quot; might be misleading, as there isn't an artifact yet that has more than five charms.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do evocations have an Essence requirement?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T13:41:27-07:00","id":922824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=922819#post922819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Do evocations have an Essence requirement?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, yes they do, so you're right on that front.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T14:28:29-07:00","id":922848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=922824#post922824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, yes they do, so you're right on that front.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wasn't really certain that was true or not. I just was making a logical assumption without double checking the Ex3 Core. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T14:38:04-07:00","id":922853,"title":"","content":"I want Warstriders that are tied to a Manse. Either by location (The 'Strider &quot;Skyforge Sentinel&quot; was crafted to guard the Skyforge Factory Cathedral, in days of old. While Skyforge lies dormant, so does it's Sentinel. Once prayers are once again hammered into shards of ice again, and the songs are sung throughout Skyforge, the Sentinel will walk again), or by slotting a specially made Hearthstone from a Manse into the 'Strider in order to power it's functions. These would, of course, represent two very different power levels, and levels of versatility: Skyforge Sentinel can only be used so long as the Factory Cathedral it is tied to is powered up, thus its power is tied directly to a location that can be damaged, shut down, etc., and so why Skyforge Sentinel would be stronger, it would be tied to a smaller area; The other 'Strider can be used anywhere in Creation that a Manse can form Hearthstones. I imagine, even a Hearthstone created by a Demesne would work, though it might make the 'Strider act oddly.<br /> <br /> I admit, I like the previous idea better than the latter. I only included the latter for those people who don't like to be tied down.<br /> <br /> I want a Warstrider that has a Tie and a Principle. The Tie could be to it's location (thus, Skyforge Sentinel has a Tie to the Skyforge), to a specific nation, or against a specific enemy. The Principle must be something that the maker of the Warstrider considered to be righteous. The 'Strider will only be piloted by someone who has a corresponding Tie and Principle, or is willing at the moment of attunement to accept such a Tie and Principle. The strength of the Tie and Principle in the character can affect the strength of the 'Strider, and unlock Evocations.<br /> <br /> Just my take, after reading through what others have said, and thinking about what I want in a Warstrider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11910-wick-black","name":"Wick Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T14:44:44-07:00","id":922858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=922685#post922685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> it needs something to give it an advantage over somethong like say Volcano Cutter which has no visible downsides to its mere existence.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not to its existence, but its greatest power is unusable if the manse where it was made is damaged, and using that power damages the manse.<br /> <br /> So I suppose there's a point for making warstrider upkeep relevant; it's not passive and mundane in the way that would only ever take place off-camera.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T15:21:08-07:00","id":922875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=922858#post922858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> Not to its existence, but its greatest power is unusable if the manse where it was made is damaged, and using that power damages the manse.<br /> <br /> So I suppose there's a point for making warstrider upkeep relevant; it's not passive and mundane in the way that would only ever take place off-camera.<br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>That is actually incorrect, only Pyroclastic Holocaust Judgement is disabled for a season, the remainder of the Evocations function as normal. Even with that accounted for it is still a Grand Daiklave which is no trivial tool.<br /> <br /> I would be fine with Warstrider Evocations before damaging in a similar fashion. The problem lies in the Warstrider having innate maintenance without sufficient advantages resulting in a situation where it would never be logical to take a warstrider over a really impressive Daiklave which wont break and can cause apocalyptic explosions once per season while still being a power weapon capable of using the majority of its powers. <br /> <br /> What I would personally like is for a warstrider to have some VERY attractive incentives that make the hassle worth it even if it is difficult. I am not against maintenance what I am against is not having a pay-off for your efforts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T15:27:34-07:00","id":922880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wick Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=922853#post922853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want a Warstrider that has a Tie and a Principle. The Tie could be to it's location (thus, Skyforge Sentinel has a Tie to the Skyforge), to a specific nation, or against a specific enemy. The Principle must be something that the maker of the Warstrider considered to be righteous. The 'Strider will only be piloted by someone who has a corresponding Tie and Principle, or is willing at the moment of attunement to accept such a Tie and Principle. The strength of the Tie and Principle in the character can affect the strength of the 'Strider, and unlock Evocations.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. I consider this an inexpressibly bad idea for the Exalted setting. Those Ties are almost certain to be completely irrelevant after centuries or millennia. Tie: the Dragonblooded. Principle: Overthrow the Celestials. Except they're already overthrown. It's too easy to make a warstrider with a tie and principle that render it useless to the PCs, and I object on priniciple to any rule that comes down to &quot;this is an easy way to rook your players.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T16:28:04-07:00","id":922906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wick Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=922853#post922853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want Warstriders that are tied to a Manse. Either by location (The 'Strider &quot;Skyforge Sentinel&quot; was crafted to guard the Skyforge Factory Cathedral, in days of old. While Skyforge lies dormant, so does it's Sentinel. Once prayers are once again hammered into shards of ice again, and the songs are sung throughout Skyforge, the Sentinel will walk again), or by slotting a specially made Hearthstone from a Manse into the 'Strider in order to power it's functions. These would, of course, represent two very different power levels, and levels of versatility: Skyforge Sentinel can only be used so long as the Factory Cathedral it is tied to is powered up, thus its power is tied directly to a location that can be damaged, shut down, etc., and so why Skyforge Sentinel would be stronger, it would be tied to a smaller area; The other 'Strider can be used anywhere in Creation that a Manse can form Hearthstones. I imagine, even a Hearthstone created by a Demesne would work, though it might make the 'Strider act oddly.<br /> <br /> I admit, I like the previous idea better than the latter. I only included the latter for those people who don't like to be tied down.<br /> <br /> <b>I want a Warstrider that has a Tie and a Principle. The Tie could be to it's location (thus, Skyforge Sentinel has a Tie to the Skyforge), to a specific nation, or against a specific enemy. The Principle must be something that the maker of the Warstrider considered to be righteous. The 'Strider will only be piloted by someone who has a corresponding Tie and Principle, or is willing at the moment of attunement to accept such a Tie and Principle. The strength of the Tie and Principle in the character can affect the strength of the 'Strider, and unlock Evocations.</b><br /> <br /> Just my take, after reading through what others have said, and thinking about what I want in a Warstrider.</div> </div> </div> </div>This could work for Bone/Hellstriders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T16:42:13-07:00","id":922911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=922875#post922875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is actually incorrect, only Pyroclastic Holocaust Judgement is disabled for a season, the remainder of the Evocations function as normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSo, you're saying that its greatest power is unusable when the manse is damaged, and that using the power damages the manse?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's too easy to make a warstrider with a tie and principle that make it useless to the PCs</div> </div> </div> </div> <i>Why?!</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T16:58:34-07:00","id":922919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=922880#post922880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. I consider this an inexpressibly bad idea for the Exalted setting. Those Ties are almost certain to be completely irrelevant after centuries or millennia. Tie: the Dragonblooded. Principle: Overthrow the Celestials. Except they're already overthrown. It's too easy to make a warstrider with a tie and principle that render it useless to the PCs, and I object on priniciple to any rule that comes down to &quot;this is an easy way to rook your players.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>But clearly they aren't overthrown just yet. As the Siddies are pulling people's strings from the shadows and Lunars are still running around causing problems. So until these are brought down there are still Celestials to overthrow.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T18:36:26-07:00","id":922968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=922911#post922911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bSo, you're saying that its greatest power is unusable when the manse is damaged, and that using the power damages the manse?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Why?!</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Wow I just realized that I misread your post, I thought that you were implying that Volcano Cutter's evocations didnt work when the manse was damaged at all, Apologies for that.<br /> <br /> My main point however is that VC is fairly devastating at most levels with only its literal nuke being locked behind a considerable charge time. If maintenance for a warstrider is going to be more punishing then a warstrider should be truly powerful even before evocations to justify a PC using it instead of just getting a 5-dot daiklave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T18:59:21-07:00","id":922984,"title":"","content":"Wait, what was I saying before about off-screen maintainence; why did I forget how the crafting system actually works?<br /> <br /> \u200bI'll grant that the question of Evocations throws some of my previously stated idea into doubt; if those qualities I described were things that had to be developed over time, it raises the question of what one does with the warstrider to begin with. I'm not talking about quantity, but quality; specific capabilities that the warstrider could have that make it more than just a big suit of armour...<br /> <br /> Unless the thing I said, with aspects akin to giant war god crushing the battle beneath its heels was a default and a commonality to all warstriders, and any Evocations it might have branch off of that central quality. Not quite a first Evocation as it is the warstrider's version of the battle stats common to all daiklaves. Given how most Evocations function, building up power as the weapon is used in its particular way, specifying its capabilities through the lens of magical material would still be something that characterises the warstrider rather than just being weapons that hang off of it. All warstriders are terrifying apparitions and crushing onslaughts of force across the field or against the walls and gates, with the Evocations as the details of its specific legendary achievements in battle, fuelled by the fervour of combat and command. The feats of accomplishment that are iconic of it in the way that certain more obvious Charms might be the iconic feats of gods and Exalted.<br /> <br /> I wonder if it's feasible for such powers to have a layer of mechanical intricacy that lets them be stronger than those of high-level Artifacts, but require a more specific and complex form of setup. Perhaps even something that is difficult to bring forth against foes of insufficient stature (which is not strictly the same as being less powerful; I imagine an unadorned Solar is still quite the challenge, but not quite of the form that gets the warstrider's heart racing).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T19:54:05-07:00","id":923013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=922911#post922911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <i>Why?!</i></div> </div> </div> </div>So the PCs can't use it, of course. Not every ST is anything resembling fair; I've met GMs for every system who absolutely delighted in every opportunity to deny the players what they wanted for their characters. I can easily see such a one letting the players plan and execute a raid for the express purpose of seizing a warstrider just to enjoy the players' reactions when they learn that it's completely useless to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T20:00:49-07:00","id":923016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=922919#post922919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But clearly they aren't overthrown just yet. As the Siddies are pulling people's strings from the shadows and Lunars are still running around causing problems. So until these are brought down there are still Celestials to overthrow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody knows about the Sidereals, so if the players want to interact with\u2026 anywhere, really, that has cities, it's useless. And if only Dragon-Blooded can use it, then it's still useless if your PCs are anything but Dragon-Blooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T20:20:58-07:00","id":923030,"title":"","content":"I think the idea of a Warstrider tied to a particular manse is cool for a one off scenario, but all Warstriders? Too limiting.<br /> <br /> I also don't like Warstriders overwriting the intimacies of the PCs or NPCs. I like the idea of Warstriders having intimacies, which may come in conflict with the character attuned to the warstrider. But make the warstrider less/more effective depending its agreement with the PCs actions rather than what is basically a ST character imposing their will on a PC. I'm not even sure I like a Warstrider initiating Social Influence on a characters. Trails too far into AI territory in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T20:52:51-07:00","id":923038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923016#post923016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nobody knows about the Sidereals, so if the players want to interact with\u2026 anywhere, really, that has cities, it's useless. And if only Dragon-Blooded can use it, then it's still useless if your PCs are anything but Dragon-Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be interesting to see a solar dealing with this sudden desire to uphold the empire, and undo the celestial exalted, when they themselves know they are one. That sort of internal conflict eating away at them from the inside might provide a sort of interesting perceptive, especially if they are made to face the ghosts of the pervious operators and come to know them, and what they stood for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T22:31:52-07:00","id":923083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=922880#post922880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. I consider this an inexpressibly bad idea for the Exalted setting. Those Ties are almost certain to be completely irrelevant after centuries or millennia. Tie: the Dragonblooded. Principle: Overthrow the Celestials. Except they're already overthrown. It's too easy to make a warstrider with a tie and principle that render it useless to the PCs, and I object on priniciple to any rule that comes down to &quot;this is an easy way to rook your players.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;No. I consider this an inexpressibly bad idea for the Exalted setting. Those Ties are almost certain to be completely irrelevant after centuries or millennia.&quot;<br /> <br /> Except, I just created one that wasn't. Also, if the Tie is irrelevant, then you have a defunct Warstrider. Tear it apart, learn how it works, and build a new one. It fits the setting.<br /> <br /> &quot;Tie: the Dragonblooded. Principle: Overthrow the Celestials. Except they're already overthrown.&quot;<br /> <br /> Fine. Tear it apart, and scavenge it for parts. Make an interesting story out ofi t.<br /> <br /> &quot;It's too easy to make a warstrider with a tie and principle that render it useless to the PCs, and I object on priniciple to any rule that comes down to &quot;this is an easy way to rook your players.&quot; &quot;<br /> <br /> They're all rules to rook the players. A Storyteller can give you a useless artifact at any time. If your storyteller is regularly giving you useless artifacts, because he can, then how can you possibly play the game?<br /> <br /> Your argument is that bad storytellers are going to be bad, so good storytellers shouldn't have a new toy to play with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11910-wick-black","name":"Wick Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T22:51:43-07:00","id":923090,"title":"","content":"No, I'm arguing that an ST option shouldn't be presented when it's much more readily used to deny a prize or reward, or worse yet make it a net loss, something that leaves a character worse off for having it. Seriously, what part of &quot;spend large amounts of time, effort and resources for an incredibly powerful artifact that we just found out we can't wield because it hates our guts&quot; sounds even slightly fun?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T22:53:08-07:00","id":923093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923090#post923090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I'm arguing that an ST option shouldn't be presented when it's much more readily used to deny a prize or reward, or worse yet make it a net loss, something that leaves a character worse off for having it. Seriously, what part of &quot;spend large amounts of time, effort and resources for an incredibly powerful artifact that we just found out we can't wield because it hates our guts&quot; sounds even slightly fun?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the problem isn't the game and the suggestions... but the people you play with, and your own mentality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T22:53:42-07:00","id":923094,"title":"","content":"That doesn't sound any fun at all. Instead of convincing me it is a bad idea, however, you have only convinced me never to play in a game run by your Storyteller.<br /> <br /> I'm done. Good day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11910-wick-black","name":"Wick Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T22:58:31-07:00","id":923097,"title":"","content":"A certain level of modularity and a potential limited intelligence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T22:58:52-07:00","id":923098,"title":"","content":"Storyteller: As you and your group finally get a whiff of the fetid air of the long-sealed tomb, your anima banners ignite and fill the room. Illuminated before you is the remarkably well preserved corpse of some giant of long ago. Sticking forth from it's shriveled breast is the hilt of a daiklave, one whose name and history are lost to time. As the Dawn Caste steps forward to claim this prize, the blade slides free, only to reveal that half the blade has been broken off. The daiklave gave its life, so the giant would be killed.<br /> <br /> Dawn Caste: So..the blade is broken?<br /> <br /> Storyteller: That's right.<br /> <br /> Dawn Caste: Is it still an artifact I can use?<br /> <br /> Storyteller: No. It's just broken.<br /> <br /> Dawn Caste: Why would you give me a broken artifact?<br /> <br /> Storyteller: ...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11910-wick-black","name":"Wick Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T23:02:58-07:00","id":923100,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think warstriders having ideals they refuse to act against is cool. I think having them force these on others is probably a bad idea. However, a Warstrider that is stronger when piloted by someone with the same ideals? Where their hearts resonate as one and yada yada CHOSEN PILOT? One that refuses to move for those who directly refute and oppose its ideals? Yeah, this is cool stuff.<br /> <br /> A warstrider with the defining principle of &quot;I must give freedom to the downtrodden', born as one of the first warstriders by a twilight in the waning days of the Primordial war, seeking to make weapons that would throw off the Primordial's grasp forever. Now it stands, refusing to operate for those who seek to exploit and control others. For the just of heart however, this great armor moves, a defender of Creaton. In the hands of ESCAPESLAVESOLARNAMEHERE, it reveals its true strengths, as their souls resonate in unity over their shared goals in life.<br /> <br /> Etc etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T23:12:08-07:00","id":923105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923100#post923100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I think warstriders having ideals they refuse to act against is cool. I think having them force these on others is probably a bad idea. However, a Warstrider that is stronger when piloted by someone with the same ideals? Where their hearts resonate as one and yada yada CHOSEN PILOT? One that refuses to move for those who directly refute and oppose its ideals? Yeah, this is cool stuff.<br /> <br /> A warstrider with the defining principle of &quot;I must give freedom to the downtrodden', born as one of the first warstriders by a twilight in the waning days of the Primordial war, seeking to make weapons that would throw off the Primordial's grasp forever. Now it stands, refusing to operate for those who seek to exploit and control others. For the just of heart however, this great armor moves, a defender of Creaton. In the hands of ESCAPESLAVESOLARNAMEHERE, it reveals its true strengths, as their souls resonate in unity over their shared goals in life.<br /> <br /> Etc etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly what I was thinking. Extra points to you for coming up with a Principle that would still be active, even in the Age of Sorrows. Especially in the Age of Sorrows. You could also give it a negative Tie against demons and the fae.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of the armor offering you a Tie and Principle, that you can choose to accept or not. Having the Tie and Principle simply makes your connection to the Warstrider stronger. Not having them, or having ones that go completely against what the 'Strider stands for, might cause problems. But they should be interesting problems, not just, &quot;The Warstrider hates you, and won't work for you.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11910-wick-black","name":"Wick Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T23:17:57-07:00","id":923107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923090#post923090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I'm arguing that an ST option shouldn't be presented when it's much more readily used to deny a prize or reward, or worse yet make it a net loss, something that leaves a character worse off for having it. Seriously, what part of &quot;spend large amounts of time, effort and resources for an incredibly powerful artifact that we just found out we can't wield because it hates our guts&quot; sounds even slightly fun?</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is the question? Does it hate your guts? No. It doesn't. It was made to uphold some ideas. The ST is not going to hand you a N/A rated artifact for just beating the pilot. He's going to make you earn it. You will have to adjust it, so the artifact gives you a positive inamacy to the Dragon Blooded, and a principal of overthrowing the Celestial exalted? That can be changed but you will need to engage in a side story of changing that idea implanted in it. <br /> <br /> Remember how I talked about talking to the souls of the pilots who came before you? All of the fragments of consciousness who fought and died in the years. Maybe you will need to convince them that you aren't evil, that they can trust you with 'Sword of Inevitable Justice'. Your not totally blocked from using it, unless you are a unimaginative player unwilling to face that the true trial is up ahead. Even then they may feel that your gaining of the 'Strider was more than likely though what they will start calling it. The 'Post Dated Cheque Loan', for how else could one of your kind with such grubby means comes into a relic this amazing except though such a debt. You will need to show them you are worthy of the newly christened 'Post Dated Cheque Loan' with your deeds, perhaps convince the specters of the previous users that their sacrifices were not in vain and that you will do many great things...or perhaps just teach them about suppressing memory and denial...either works.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T00:43:08-07:00","id":923125,"title":"","content":"I want warstriders to actually have their own health levels (like hull for ships) and legendary size merit for sure. I dont like them modeled as slightly large armors. You'll get piloting penalty when you oparate a damaged warstrider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T02:53:19-07:00","id":923148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923013#post923013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the PCs can't use it, of course. Not every ST is anything resembling fair; I've met GMs for every system who absolutely delighted in every opportunity to deny the players what they wanted for their characters. I can easily see such a one letting the players plan and execute a raid for the express purpose of seizing a warstrider just to enjoy the players' reactions when they learn that it's completely useless to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not really something that is enabled by warstriders having qualities that align with Intimacies, or prevented by them not. I don't think rules should be based on what arbitrarily dickish Storytellers would do with them.<br /> <br /> I've really got to ask why any players would tolerate such management.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's much more readily used to deny</div> </div> </div> </div> I find you to be begging the question.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 06-29-2016, 05:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T04:02:44-07:00","id":923162,"title":"","content":"I want to be able to customize my warstrider with <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/CombatStilettos\" target=\"_blank\">combat stillettos</a>, <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ShoulderCannon\" target=\"_blank\">shoulder cannon</a>, and <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TorpedoTits\" target=\"_blank\">more</a>. I want them to be the best and most outrageous choice for fighting a behemoth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T04:54:58-07:00","id":923173,"title":"","content":"I kind of prefer warstriders as a status symbol and place of arcane power, like a Manse with legs. Actually using them in combat gets messy really quickly, as playing the Mechwarrior RPG taught me. I like them as symbols of the pilot's glory, rather than as an actual combat-capable mech. This might differ from my previously stated preferences, but I've given it extra thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T05:49:05-07:00","id":923195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923148#post923148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is not really something that is enabled by warstriders having qualities that align with Intimacies, or prevented by them not. I don't think rules should be based on what arbitrarily dickish Storytellers would do with them.<br /> <br /> I've really got to ask why any players would tolerate such management.<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> I find you to be begging the question.<br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>I think you've already answered it. If I look at a proposed rule, and my very first thought is &quot;this is pathetically easy to abuse,&quot; then I consider it a bad proposal. Yes, an ST could use such a rule to enable cool things, but it's far easier to use that rule to justify frustrating and useless things. People can be amazingly petty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T05:51:31-07:00","id":923197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ncolic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923125#post923125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want warstriders to actually have their own health levels (like hull for ships) and legendary size merit for sure. I dont like them modeled as slightly large armors. You'll get piloting penalty when you oparate a damaged warstrider.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree entirely. They should have their own soak, hardness, health tracks and Strength score.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T06:00:54-07:00","id":923200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923195#post923195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I look at a proposed rule, and my very first thought is &quot;this is pathetically easy to abuse,&quot; then I consider it a bad proposal. Yes, an ST could use such a rule to enable cool things, but it's far easier to use that rule to justify frustrating and useless things. People can be amazingly petty.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bDo you apply this complaint to the actual Intimacy rules? Do you see social influence purely through the lens of Storytellers who are so uninterested in telling stories that they will only ever give players non-player characters whose Ties and Principles cannot be appealed to in the least by such players, basically cutting them off entirely from social influence as gameplay?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T06:02:14-07:00","id":923201,"title":"","content":"I concur that it's best to write rules that provide the best median outcome. Some groups will ruin things and others will make them awesome, but you can only really account for people who will play the rules as read, and if the rules as read are too open to abuse, they'll be abused as a starting point, rather than as the outcome of a particularly &quot;bad&quot; group of players/ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T06:15:45-07:00","id":923204,"title":"","content":"I like the idea that a Warstrider could have intimacies. I just don't like the idea of the Warstrider imposing these intimacies on the Pilot as a requirement to attune. Attuning to a Warstrider shouldn't require an End User Agreement of &quot;You will enact revenge upon those murdering Usurpers&quot;. If your character's intimacies align with the Warstriders, that's great! If not, well that make good drama. <br /> <br /> Intimacies should grow organically, not be something you can add to your character for access to a cool artifact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T09:05:20-07:00","id":923290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ncolic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923125#post923125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want warstriders to actually have their own health levels (like hull for ships) and legendary size merit for sure. I don't like them modeled as slightly large armors. You'll get piloting penalty when you operate a damaged warstrider.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that bonus Health Levels would be a more tenable middle ground, as would some static bonuses/penalties to certain Physical rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T09:25:27-07:00","id":923299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923290#post923290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that bonus Health Levels would be a more tenable middle ground, as would some static bonuses/penalties to certain Physical rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>From a reason stand point why would I use my strength at all, a 'strider pilot in their machine should use its strength, but their Dexterity. Also since damaged artifacts are now more of a thing I have to add my support to strikers having hull points infact I think that might be a good system for all &quot;vehicles&quot; including charriots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T09:34:38-07:00","id":923306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923148#post923148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've really got to ask why any players would tolerate such management.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lack of other options. This hobby is relatively rare, especially face to face, and STs rarer still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T09:37:46-07:00","id":923308,"title":"","content":"It seems plausible that their 3rd edition's incarnation will be a lot less mecha and more golem-armor-like, I think?<br /> <br /> Anyway, regardless of the level of magitech, I would like to see Warstriders as impresive artificial titans not limited to humanoid form. And, since even a single daiklave can have as much destruction power as Volcano Cutter (I know that's an art 5), imagine how much power a walking battle tank could have!!! Speaking of walking battle tanks... I'll be happy if I can get enough rules to make an &quot;Orichalcum Gear&quot;, capable of blasting cities from one Elemental Pole to any other. Then it's upt to Night Caste Snake, and his Twilight partner Otacon, to stop Day Caste Liquid and his infernal corps from taking over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T09:45:41-07:00","id":923313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wick Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923094#post923094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> however, you have only convinced me never to play in a game run by your Storyteller.</div> </div> </div> </div> Can we try not to respond like this in future? It doesn't make the conversation go anywhere good.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T09:57:50-07:00","id":923319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923308#post923308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems plausible that their 3rd edition's incarnation will be a lot less mecha and more golem-armor-like, I think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought they had gone the exact opposite way with 3rd ed. Warstriders are now rarer and more precious, and more precious generally means BIGGER. I also got that impression from the picture of Warstriders on parade in the corebook (let me get home and i'll add the page for reference)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T10:08:15-07:00","id":923329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923319#post923319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought they had gone the exact opposite way with 3rd ed. Warstriders are now rarer and more precious, and more precious generally means BIGGER. I also got that impression from the picture of Warstriders on parade in the corebook (let me get home and i'll add the page for reference)</div> </div> </div> </div>True. I was refering mainly to how their &quot;inner mechanism&quot; will be described, maybe a bit less gears and capacitors and shit, and more motion runes, spiritual core, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T11:11:54-07:00","id":923373,"title":"","content":"Really, even Second Edition's description of the most powerful and intricate warstriders had it that their internal workings consisted of expertly crafted and sanctified springs and bars and things.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat's a level of detail I would still rather avoid.<br /> <br /> \u200bIndeed, I would honestly find a load of technobabble based on vaguely fantasy terms to be almost as bad as capacitors and what have you. <br /> <br /> Ultimately, the cosmetics of the thing are the least significant and most easily adjusted, unless somebody asking for it to be like a Macross Valkyrie or even Escaflowne has some specific mechanical distinction to that in mind that is wholly irreconcilable with the Iron Golem.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T11:23:08-07:00","id":923379,"title":"","content":"Any and all technobabble on the function of artifacts should be produced by players during craft stunts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T14:01:34-07:00","id":923469,"title":"","content":"Based on earlier dev comments, I suspect that Warstrider will simply be a term for <i>any</i> sort of giant armor that people pilot around rather than for a specific type of giant mobile armor as was the case in 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> Some warstriders might be magical golems composed of rock and stone or wood and metal. Others might be like large automatons, crafted from complex clockwork and gears. Yet others could be formed from still-living demons, or made from necromantically animated bone and sinew with plenty of bone-jacking possibilities, or even unique wyld-behemoths you can don like armor.<br /> <br /> Ultimately all of these Warstriders will share similar statistics and any differences will largely be secondary - for example, a warstrider made out of rock might repair itself by sinking into the earth for 5 days, or one made out of demons might have a unique ability that allows its screams to instill fear into those who hear it. But the core capabilities and statistics of Warstriders will be fairly similar regardless of how or what they are constructed from.<br /> <br /> I imagine that the most &quot;common&quot; type of Warstrider will continue to be the Escaflowne-inspired ones that we saw back in First Edition, but likely the gameline will be clear that Warstriders can take almost any form and be created from almost any type of material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T14:57:48-07:00","id":923504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wick Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923098#post923098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Storyteller: As you and your group finally get a whiff of the fetid air of the long-sealed tomb, your anima banners ignite and fill the room. Illuminated before you is the remarkably well preserved corpse of some giant of long ago. Sticking forth from it's shriveled breast is the hilt of a daiklave, one whose name and history are lost to time. As the Dawn Caste steps forward to claim this prize, the blade slides free, only to reveal that half the blade has been broken off. The daiklave gave its life, so the giant would be killed.<br /> <br /> Dawn Caste: So..the blade is broken?<br /> <br /> Storyteller: That's right.<br /> <br /> Dawn Caste: Is it still an artifact I can use?<br /> <br /> Storyteller: No. It's just broken.<br /> <br /> Dawn Caste: Why would you give me a broken artifact?<br /> <br /> Storyteller: ...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That honestly just gave me a kind of awesome idea for an artifact/plot. A broken Grand Daiklaive where the break was clean(ish) enough for the weapon to still be used as a somewhat unwieldy smaller Daiklaive (Either regular or maybe a Reaver Daiklaive). The wielder could either just choose to leave it in its broken state, or hunt for the remaining pieces and have the blade reforged, returning it to a Grand Daiklaive and unlocking any potential Evocations it might have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T15:01:35-07:00","id":923507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923504#post923504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That honestly just gave me a kind of awesome idea for an artifact/plot. A broken Grand Daiklaive where the break was clean(ish) enough for the weapon to still be used as a somewhat unwieldy smaller Daiklaive (Either regular or maybe a Reaver Daiklaive). The wielder could either just choose to leave it in its broken state, or hunt for the remaining pieces and have the blade reforged, returning it to a Grand Daiklaive and unlocking any potential Evocations it might have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I came up with the same idea! It could have Evocations of being unbreakable, but with a single, fatal flaw. Or, Evocations of sacrifice, making it easier for the bearer to protect others, by sacrificing themself. I love it!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11910-wick-black","name":"Wick Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T15:19:07-07:00","id":923518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wick Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923507#post923507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I came up with the same idea! It could have Evocations of being unbreakable, but with a single, fatal flaw. Or, Evocations of sacrifice, making it easier for the bearer to protect others, by sacrificing themself. I love it!</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooooo, I like it.<br /> <br /> And statting the base artifact would be super easy. Just knock off one of the tags to get across the &quot;it's broken and not working as intended&quot; (either Balanced or Chopping, depending on how you want the vibe of the busted sword to be), but they still get the artifact base stats, which are stupid good as is.<br /> <br /> Could even add a twist on the &quot;fix it&quot; angle, too. Rather than trying to hunt down it's pieces, there's still enough material that a gifted crafter could work the material into the &quot;lesser&quot; form, kind of like the reshaping of Valyrian Steel in A Song of Ice and Fire. Maybe doing so returns the relevant tag, but cuts off access to the highest tier Evocations, or maybe opens a path to all new ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":882,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","user":"SamuraiMujuru","date":". 06-29-2016, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T16:50:53-07:00","id":923569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923299#post923299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From a reason stand point why would I use my strength at all, a 'strider pilot in their machine should use its strength, but their Dexterity. Also since damaged artifacts are now more of a thing I have to add my support to strikers having hull points infact I think that might be a good system for all &quot;vehicles&quot; including charriots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just going off of an admittedly 2e understanding of how warstriders are piloted, e.g.: there's a haptic linkage rather than a bunch of buttons, knobs, and switches, a la Escaflowne. There's a raw physicality necessary that relying entirely of the suit just doesn't capture. Also, it's a lot of unnecessary book keeping to have two sets of stats, that would do little to discourage using the Warstrider to solve most, if not all, of your combat problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T18:14:07-07:00","id":923602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923569#post923569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it's a lot of unnecessary book keeping to have two sets of stats, that would do little to discourage using the Warstrider to solve most, if not all, of your combat problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the new charm system didn't discourage the new player, i dont think a simple additional health / attack pool track are gonna discourage anyone (heck you keep a different attack pool between two weapons already). Also you always used a fixed strength when using a warstrider; 12/16/20 if my memory is correct for different models.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T19:07:07-07:00","id":923631,"title":"","content":"I want a Warstrider fight to be reminiscent of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yg3mSqyz30s\" target=\"_blank\">Big O vs Big Duo</a>, with slow, ponderous but nigh-invincible and overwhelmingly powerful god-mechs tearing apart the geography with the simple act of exchanging blows.<br /> <br /> Alternately, I want them to be like an <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xSZZXV_vlFY\" target=\"_blank\">Armored Core</a> match with the energy set to infinity. Blindingly fast and impossible for mortals to keep up with, and even the slightest mistake can mean the difference between victory and defeat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","user":"JayTee","date":". 06-29-2016, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T19:10:15-07:00","id":923632,"title":"","content":"One problem with making it strength but not say, dexterity or stamina or wits or etc agnostic is that it creates a system where it's further made evident that raising your dexterity is 100% the better decision, rather than raising your strength. Any character with a warstrider will be expected to just dump their strength, and be scrawny outside it, because hey, it doesn't matter if I have 1 str or 5 str when my mech always has 20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T19:32:28-07:00","id":923637,"title":"","content":"And that's yet another reason to set up warstrider deployment as a Godzilla threshold decision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T20:29:13-07:00","id":923663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923632#post923632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One problem with making it strength but not say, dexterity or stamina or wits or etc agnostic is that it creates a system where it's further made evident that raising your dexterity is 100% the better decision, rather than raising your strength. Any character with a warstrider will be expected to just dump their strength, and be scrawny outside it, because hey, it doesn't matter if I have 1 str or 5 str when my mech always has 20.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of the &quot;less crazy&quot; mechs have usually taken a huge toll on their pilots. Battlemechs in the Battletech universe overheat, making piloting one like sitting in a sauna on the best of days, so Mechwarriors tend to be in peak physical condition. Escaflowne and other Melefs/Guymelefs clearly require the pilot to put forth a lot of effort to get the huge beast moving. It'd make sense that have some kind of physical minimums just to be able to get the thing to move, not unlike strength minimums on weapons in prior editions.<br /> <br /> Could also do some kind of resistance roll periodically to see if the physical exertion doesn't make them pass out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":882,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","user":"SamuraiMujuru","date":". 06-29-2016, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T21:18:42-07:00","id":923694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923632#post923632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One problem with making it strength but not say, dexterity or stamina or wits or etc agnostic is that it creates a system where it's further made evident that raising your dexterity is 100% the better decision, rather than raising your strength. Any character with a warstrider will be expected to just dump their strength, and be scrawny outside it, because hey, it doesn't matter if I have 1 str or 5 str when my mech always has 20.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which, as I stated, doesn't mesh with how warstrider piloting is represented in earlier editions in the fluff. Fatigue is gone from the system as a consideration in combat, so the difficulty inherent to prolonged warstrider combat can't be the balancing factor to warstriders as part of the Circle's arsenal anymore, at least, not without bringing back those considerations. It leads back to the issue that the Devs were trying to avoid: having a clearly superior option that makes all others pale in comparison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T21:44:23-07:00","id":923697,"title":"","content":"I have not given Warstriders much detailed thought yet, but I do have a few generalities for how I currently envision them:<br /> <br /> I would like it if Warstriders in general had a clear primary purpose of being used against armies, giant monsters and geographic features. They shouldn't be useless in personal combat against a single formidable human sized enemy, but I'd like to see them somewhat out of scale for such a foe.<br /> <br /> I imagine that achieved primarily by making their stronger powers overkill against a single normal-sized person, and costed appropriately for that large scale, in resources like essence/willpower and/or tactical restrictions like set-ups (similar to Volcano Cutter, for example), charging time, difficult reset conditions, lower accuracy against small targets except in certain circumstances, et cetera. For instance, a hit-everything-in-a-mile Evocation that costs a lot of motes or requires quite a bit of set-up or charging or whatever to execute, when you really don't need to hit everything in a mile if your opponent is a single person.<br /> <br /> They should still have normal attacks and often lesser powers/Evocations that are appropriate for a fight against a dangerous normal-sized enemy, But I'd prefer if their best powers are usually too wasteful, large-scale, costly, and/or hard to use that it is often not worth applying for things other than vaporizing vast armies, mountains, Behemoths and things like that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ideally, I would also like for them to feel a bit slow and clumsy, but powerful and hard to put down, compared to a similarly skilled character that is not in a Warstrider, unless that particular Strider's gimmick is exactly in being super fast/agile/mobile for such a huge thing, of course (though that probably means it has less in powers of utter destruction and invulnerability). Not sure if that feeling would just be a matter of stats like accuracy bonuses, mobility penalties, damage and soak/hardness or if some other mechanic would be needed to really make it feel right during play.<br /> <br /> Of course, a Solar with the right charms if gonna minimize or eliminate most of that relative clumsiness, but that investment could be going somewhere else and that else could be where a non-warstrider Solar gets the edge they need against the larger opponent.<br /> <br /> Finally, I want a &quot;pankration&quot; match between a DB brawler in a Warstrider and a Brawl/Resistance Solar to be an epic, drawn-out, slug-and-smash-fest for the ages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T21:45:28-07:00","id":923699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923663#post923663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A lot of the &quot;less crazy&quot; mechs have usually taken a huge toll on their pilots. Battlemechs in the Battletech universe overheat, making piloting one like sitting in a sauna on the best of days, so Mechwarriors tend to be in peak physical condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>A 'Mech or Aerospace Fighter is uncomfortable. Any other type of typical combat unit, however, is a flaming death trap waiting to be hit by inferno missiles or plasma rounds. As it turns out, tracking heat is actually an advantage.<br /> <br /> (Infernos were even more vicious in prior editions, where instead of automatically critting they would potentially just kill a conventional vehicle outright).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T21:54:34-07:00","id":923702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923699#post923699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A 'Mech or Aerospace Fighter is uncomfortable. Any other type of typical combat unit, however, is a flaming death trap waiting to be hit by inferno missiles or plasma rounds. As it turns out, tracking heat is actually an advantage.<br /> <br /> (Infernos were even more vicious in prior editions, where instead of automatically critting they would potentially just kill a conventional vehicle outright).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True, though infernos were pants-shittingly terrifying to Mech pilots, to, especially in lighter Mechs. Tended to overheat things bad enough that even the auto shutdown kicked the bucket and the pilot just cooked alive. There's a whole big thing about it in Decision At Thunder Rift, and it's how Grayson Death Carlisle captures the first mech in the soon to be Grey Death Legion (And meets his wife! Romance by nearly cooking them alive, good times.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T22:20:07-07:00","id":923712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923702#post923702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> True, though infernos were pants-shittingly terrifying to Mech pilots, to, especially in lighter Mechs. Tended to overheat things bad enough that even the auto shutdown kicked the bucket and the pilot just cooked alive. There's a whole big thing about it in Decision At Thunder Rift, and it's how Grayson Death Carlisle captures the first mech in the soon to be Grey Death Legion (And meets his wife! Romance by nearly cooking them alive, good times.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That wasn't really mechanically defined until TacOps and the expanded heat scale, though. Ammo explosions would probably get you first; machine gun ammo in particular is like carrying a WMD-grade bomb that's heat-sensitive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T23:35:09-07:00","id":923734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923712#post923712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That wasn't really mechanically defined until TacOps and the expanded heat scale, though. Ammo explosions would probably get you first; machine gun ammo in particular is like carrying a WMD-grade bomb that's heat-sensitive.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but I also wasn't referencing hard mechanics. I was referencing narrative and setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T06:28:41-07:00","id":923811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923694#post923694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fatigue is gone from the system as a consideration in combat...</div> </div> </div> </div>Fatigue generally wasn't a combat-scale consideration in the system in previous editions, either; checks for it occurred in hours or (in the most absolutely strenuous conditions) minutes, and in my years of playing, most combats generally ended in so many seconds (even if they took like four hours to resolve).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-30-2016, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T06:37:55-07:00","id":923815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923702#post923702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, though infernos were pants-shittingly terrifying to Mech pilots, to, especially in lighter Mechs. Tended to overheat things bad enough that even the auto shutdown kicked the bucket and the pilot just cooked alive. There's a whole big thing about it in Decision At Thunder Rift, and it's how Grayson Death Carlisle captures the first mech in the soon to be Grey Death Legion (And meets his wife! Romance by nearly cooking them alive, good times.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh hey, someone else who read those novels!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T07:42:35-07:00","id":923848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923569#post923569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just going off of an admittedly 2e understanding of how warstriders are piloted, e.g.: there's a haptic linkage rather than a bunch of buttons, knobs, and switches, a la Escaflowne. There's a raw physicality necessary that relying entirely of the suit just doesn't capture. Also, it's a lot of unnecessary book keeping to have two sets of stats, that would do little to discourage using the Warstrider to solve most, if not all, of your combat problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having a almost QC sheet for your strider where it's weapons, soak, and health track are isn't that much book keeping. more over the controls for the strider were almost described as wires connected to your body and gloves with wires connected to them so that as you moved the wires fed back the information, but you were acting with the strider's strength not your own, and this system favors Dex and without the merit that lets you make melee attacks with your strength like 1e and 2e then you are probably going to focus more and dex than strength anyway. But I agree setting a minimum strength for operating is reasonable. <br /> More over in the battle tech examples above the 'Mech is piloted with the use of a Neurohelmet that captures your thoughts and relays them to the machine so that the thought lift arm translates to ...lift the arm. What I personally might like to see is a 'Strider Control skill. Even if it's something like Ride, or sail, or something that makes it so that while punching with the strider is your brawl, staying balanced when someone else hits you, or footing isn't as good would be nice. <br /> <br /> Plus of course if 'Strider's had operational time limits, limited by a sort of fuel reserve might be interesting. I know that's a little Iron Kingdoms, where your Warjack has only 30 minutes of combat time before it runs out of coal, and not something I think every strider should have but an option for a broken blade style &quot;oh crap I pushed too hard too long&quot; and the 'Strider is powered down to recover it's essence reserve or burned out your last hearth stone and those will need a day to recover might be interesting and create some good drama. Or invoke battle tech with the heat scale and suddenly while the strider can march all day and night the moment it hits combat it starts to build up &quot;heat&quot; and risks shutting down to cool off. All of these sort of 'flaws' would make a strider a suboptimal option for every situation but for things like sieging a city, fighting something giant, or fighting a war, then the 'strider should be allowed to shine but not be so good it makes it the only choice. Which is where maybe giving us a list of flaws like overheat, limited fuel, fatigue, difficult controls would allow us to design 'Striders that are great options but not without some reasons other than space why you can't use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T08:25:40-07:00","id":923863,"title":"","content":"Do you think still needing a linked hearthstone slotted in it is a good idea or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T08:37:35-07:00","id":923870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923863#post923863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think still needing a linked hearthstone slotted in it is a good idea or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it should be an optional consideration for striders, One that might give benefits, but basically be a drawback to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T09:44:59-07:00","id":923912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923870#post923870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it should be an optional consideration for striders, One that might give benefits, but basically be a drawback to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps a requirement to use Evocations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T09:57:12-07:00","id":923918,"title":"","content":"Idea: a Warstrider that runs on Sorcerous Motes. Good news: it doesn't require a hearthstone to operate. Bad news: requires a Sorcerer to pilot, who needs to make periodic Shape Sorcery rolls to keep the thing running, and would have pretty hefty SM commitments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T10:19:55-07:00","id":923926,"title":"","content":"Warstriders ought to be power hogs. Committed Essence and hearthstones, possibly multiple stones, fit perfectly with my conception of them as being huge, powerful, and nearly unstoppable, but also finicky, high maintenance, and extremely power-hungry. As I've said, Warstriders should be for Godzilla threshold situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T10:28:00-07:00","id":923931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923863#post923863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think still needing a linked hearthstone slotted in it is a good idea or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Escaflowne and other melefs operate with wildborn stones created within the hearts of dragons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T10:37:36-07:00","id":923947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923162#post923162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to be able to customize my warstrider with <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/CombatStilettos\" target=\"_blank\">combat stillettos</a>, <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ShoulderCannon\" target=\"_blank\">shoulder cannon</a>, and <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TorpedoTits\" target=\"_blank\">more</a>. I want them to be the best and most outrageous choice for fighting a behemoth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have profoundly missed your posts, Jut.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T10:54:35-07:00","id":923963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923912#post923912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps a requirement to use Evocations?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well as one other person mentioned not for all striders. Some should run on Sorcerers motes and require that a sorcerer makes periodic checks to channel in socererous motes. I think some striders should yes, just like I think some striders should require an intimacy to be fired up, and some should imprint one on the pilot. I think that some should even not require a stone or sorcerous motes but instead have a internal pool of energy that takes time to build up, and using the evocations depletes this pool faster, and faster. I think some should require surgically implanted parts of a control system or demon ink tattoos (for infernal striders) that act as a part of the control system and allow the user to make use of some (not all, and not at full power) evocations even while not inside the strider because of a permanent bond. I think some striders should have problems with over heating where their evocations generate heat as well as making attack actions and other certain actions do, and these striders can vent the heat but when it reaches a certain point they shut down. I think these draw backs would be fun, and I think every strider should have 1 of them. Maybe 2...but 1 seems fine. I think each of these drawbacks should grant it's own unique advantage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T13:14:07-07:00","id":924056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923863#post923863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think still needing a linked hearthstone slotted in it is a good idea or not?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've always been really mixed on the Hearthstone as power sources. Manses/Hearthstones are supposed to be at least moderately rare, and I always hate having to hand players a bunch of extra powers just because they want to use their cool toy. My groups have always created artifacts that are pretty much just hearthstones minus the magic for the purpose of powering things like Warstriders.<br /> <br /> But, on the flip side, it makes sense to have some manner of extra requirement to power the immortal god armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T15:56:18-07:00","id":924151,"title":"","content":"In Oadenol's Codex the writers explicitly state that almost nobody in Creation is more than a week's ride from a demesne, and most people only two or three. That comes out to probably a hundred miles between demesnes, and that means that Creation holds tens of thousands of demesnes, some capped, some not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T16:01:59-07:00","id":924154,"title":"","content":"If, and this is a big if, I had my dream, Hearthstones that power Warstriders would -do- things to the warstriders. Like, using a Freedom Stone to power a warstrider would give it access to a separate set of evocations, not Warstrider Evocations, not the Hearthstone evocations, but something unique and thematic. A solar hearthstone filled Warstrider would glow with the awesome might of the sun coursing through its frame, even if it was made of Jade, while a fire one would blaze with great fire, or a sidereal essence one be given a prismatic arrangement of shields etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T19:24:25-07:00","id":924232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=924154#post924154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If, and this is a big if, I had my dream, Hearthstones that power Warstriders would -do- things to the warstriders. Like, using a Freedom Stone to power a warstrider would give it access to a separate set of evocations, not Warstrider Evocations, not the Hearthstone evocations, but something unique and thematic. A solar hearthstone filled Warstrider would glow with the awesome might of the sun coursing through its frame, even if it was made of Jade, while a fire one would blaze with great fire, or a sidereal essence one be given a prismatic arrangement of shields etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't agree more. I think that is something that should be, and would be the upside to a hearthstone draw back, for requiring a hearthstone to power the 'Strider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T16:42:11-07:00","id":924674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=923013#post923013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the PCs can't use it, of course. Not every ST is anything resembling fair; I've met GMs for every system who absolutely delighted in every opportunity to deny the players what they wanted for their characters. I can easily see such a one letting the players plan and execute a raid for the express purpose of seizing a warstrider just to enjoy the players' reactions when they learn that it's completely useless to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I loathe this &quot;GM vs Players&quot; mentality with a fiery-hot intensity. Absolutely detest it. It's part of why I've made statements about how if a ST lets you invest points of some kind in an artifact and evocations, and then destroys the artifact without any form of refund, that ST is a jerk who honestly shouldn't be running a game.<br /> <br /> I'll just say that if a person looks at a rule and says &quot;Oh GOOD, I can thoroughly dick over and destroy the hopes of my players with this&quot;, then the problem isn't the rule. No amount of rules finagling will keep that mindset from fucking the players over. They will find a way. There's a difference between toying around with Characters for the sake of drama, and ruining the fun of the PLAYERS. One of my big things for my players is &quot;If they're not having fun, I'm not having fun&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, about Warstriders with Intimacies... I wouldn't make EVERY Warstrider have them, but I like the idea of some Warstriders were built for some purpose. Maybe it'd be something like how with Black Wind, it unlocks its Evocations for someone who acts in a certain way. Maybe a Warstrider would grant Evocations to a pilot that upholds one of the Warstrider's Intimacies. I wouldn't go so far as to say ALL Striders should. But hell, personally? I'd like room for it. I'd like for Evocations, materials, and construction aesthetics to allow the Warstriders to be as varied as artifact weapons so far.<br /> <br /> Like, technically Spring Razor and Beloved Adorei are both daiklaves. But their Evocations make them look and feel distinct from one-another. I'd like that with Warstriders. I'd like a system wherein one person can say that they stand in the chest cavity of a massive terracotta colossus inscribed with prayers to the Unconquered Sun, so that the Warstrider awakens and moves while in the sunlight, and another person can put together whirling gears, pounding pistons, hissing steam vents, and gets all Super Robot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T18:32:14-07:00","id":924704,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I like the image of a magic crystal being placed into a slot to power these kinds of things, but I also think it's an insignificant enough detail that, apart from providing no other powers (besides possibly the native magic of the hearthstone), I would often just assume the warstrider just comes with it (in a narrative, if not a literal sense), especially if one can have hearthstones that are not dependent on manses now.<br /> <br /> \u200bI feel as though this is an admission that the former is a largely cosmetic issue that can readily be dropped without a problem, so not really worth advocating for. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T18:41:46-07:00","id":924707,"title":"","content":"I would like a sub system like they have for ships.<br /> Something that can be effected by normal combat just not commonly. Also i would like to avoid them just being bigger and better armors and/or weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11915-wandering-swordman","name":"Wandering Swordman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11915_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T18:44:17-07:00","id":924709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=924674#post924674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">one person can say that they stand in the chest cavity of a massive terracotta colossus inscribed with prayers to the Unconquered Sun, so that the Warstrider awakens and moves while in the sunlight, and another person can put together whirling gears, pounding pistons, hissing steam vents, and gets all Super Robot.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWebpage reloaded for no reason while looking over complleed post and decideeeeeeeinhg inf Anything else was needed. very annoyed<br /> <br /> I like the idea that if modern person opened up waerstrider of any cosmetic, theinterna l mechanisms would be wholly incomprehwnsible and if there's any difference betwweeen trracotra and stem than a modern observer would not be able to discern it<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T18:44:22-07:00","id":924710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=924674#post924674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I loathe this &quot;GM vs Players&quot; mentality with a fiery-hot intensity. Absolutely detest it. It's part of why I've made statements about how if a ST lets you invest points of some kind in an artifact and evocations, and then destroys the artifact without any form of refund, that ST is a jerk who honestly shouldn't be running a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I agree. But there are a lot of awful STs out there, and the fact that they'll find ways to torment their players no matter what's in the rules is just that much more reason not to hand them obvious clubs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T18:45:04-07:00","id":924711,"title":"","content":"Your obvious club is my table leg.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T18:48:27-07:00","id":924715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=924674#post924674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I loathe this &quot;GM vs Players&quot; mentality with a fiery-hot intensity. Absolutely detest it. It's part of why I've made statements about how if a ST lets you invest points of some kind in an artifact and evocations, and then destroys the artifact without any form of refund, that ST is a jerk who honestly shouldn't be running a game.<br /> <br /> I'll just say that if a person looks at a rule and says &quot;Oh GOOD, I can thoroughly dick over and destroy the hopes of my players with this&quot;, then the problem isn't the rule. No amount of rules finagling will keep that mindset from fucking the players over. They will find a way. There's a difference between toying around with Characters for the sake of drama, and ruining the fun of the PLAYERS. One of my big things for my players is &quot;If they're not having fun, I'm not having fun&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, about Warstriders with Intimacies... I wouldn't make EVERY Warstrider have them, but I like the idea of some Warstriders were built for some purpose. Maybe it'd be something like how with Black Wind, it unlocks its Evocations for someone who acts in a certain way. Maybe a Warstrider would grant Evocations to a pilot that upholds one of the Warstrider's Intimacies. I wouldn't go so far as to say ALL Striders should. But hell, personally? I'd like room for it. I'd like for Evocations, materials, and construction aesthetics to allow the Warstriders to be as varied as artifact weapons so far.<br /> <br /> Like, technically Spring Razor and Beloved Adorei are both daiklaves. But their Evocations make them look and feel distinct from one-another. I'd like that with Warstriders. I'd like a system wherein one person can say that they stand in the chest cavity of a massive terracotta colossus inscribed with prayers to the Unconquered Sun, so that the Warstrider awakens and moves while in the sunlight, and another person can put together whirling gears, pounding pistons, hissing steam vents, and gets all Super Robot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very well stated. Also the reason I don't get into such arguments, because they are frankly ridiculous.<br /> <br /> Everything you said from &quot;Warstriders with Intimacies&quot; down is perfect. Exactly what I want, as well. Warstriders are magic. They can be magitech, but they don't have to be. I love that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11910-wick-black","name":"Wick Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T19:21:11-07:00","id":924725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=924674#post924674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I loathe this &quot;GM vs Players&quot; mentality with a fiery-hot intensity. Absolutely detest it. It's part of why I've made statements about how if a ST lets you invest points of some kind in an artifact and evocations, and then destroys the artifact without any form of refund, that ST is a jerk who honestly shouldn't be running a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>It works in some RPGs. Old school dungeon crawlers and the like were meant to be more akin to tactical wargames and pit the players and the dungeon master against one another. Exalted though? Not so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T20:01:05-07:00","id":924740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=924709#post924709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bWebpage reloaded for no reason while looking over complleed post and decideeeeeeeinhg inf Anything else was needed. very annoyed<br /> <br /> I like the idea that if modern person opened up waerstrider of any cosmetic, theinterna l mechanisms would be wholly incomprehwnsible and if there's any difference betwweeen trracotra and stem than a modern observer would not be able to discern it</div> </div> </div> </div>Building on this: I imagine that if you don't get trained by someone else who knows how to pilot that one particular warstrider, there's a lot of trial and error involved. And if you know how to pilot a melef-type interface suit Strider, then when you get into one where you kneel in a circle and meditate to project your awareness in... It'll be a penalty until you can overcome the unfamiliar layout.<br /> <br /> <i>Sol help you </i>if you get one with buttons and levers. Your first outing in THAT Warstrider will look like someone playing QWOP","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T21:19:33-07:00","id":924762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=924711#post924711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your obvious club is my table leg.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you think Warstriders in your game ought to have Ties and Principles that the pilots must satisfy, that's fine. But I still oppose it being made the official default because, as by now I hope I've made clear, I consider it to be far too readily abused. Solar PCs? All the Warstriders have Tie: Dragon-Blooded. They'll never serve the PCs. These were literally my first thoughts. That to me is an extremely clear indicator of a bad default rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T21:36:34-07:00","id":924766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=924740#post924740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Building on this: I imagine that if you don't get trained by someone else who knows how to pilot that one particular warstrider, there's a lot of trial and error involved. And if you know how to pilot a melef-type interface suit Strider, then when you get into one where you kneel in a circle and meditate to project your awareness in... It'll be a penalty until you can overcome the unfamiliar layout.<br /> <br /> <i>Sol help you </i>if you get one with buttons and levers. Your first outing in THAT Warstrider will look like someone playing QWOP</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am reminded of a rather embarrassing moment at a game once.<br /> <br /> The players had just discovered an ancient and powerful First Age prototype Warstrider - I called it the Mindstrider. Yeah, I'd been rewatching Macross Plus. Anyway, it had a sort of &quot;mental control&quot;system which allowed the owner to operate it purely through using their mind. There was a port interface in which the owner would insert their hand, close their eyes and then the Warstrider would respond to their every move. Now that I think about it, it didn't actually <i>do</i> anything, but I thought it sounded cool at the time...<br /> <br /> So I explained all this to the players when they managed to read the schematics, &quot;And then you put one of your extremities inside the port, close your eyes and the Warstrider will magically transfer all of the outside stimulus to your characters mind.&quot;<br /> <br /> One of my players looks at me and says, &quot;An extremity? You mean I gotta like, put my penis in there?&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, everyone at the table busts up laughing and I throw up my hands, &quot;No you asshole, one of your <i>hands!</i>. HANDS!&quot;<br /> <br /> But the damage was done. Forever after everyone referred to it as the Cockstrider with a built in penis-port.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T00:02:32-07:00","id":924795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=924766#post924766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I am reminded of a rather embarrassing moment at a game once.<br /> <br /> The players had just discovered an ancient and powerful First Age prototype Warstrider - I called it the Mindstrider. Yeah, I'd been rewatching Macross Plus. Anyway, it had a sort of &quot;mental control&quot;system which allowed the owner to operate it purely through using their mind. There was a port interface in which the owner would insert their hand, close their eyes and then the Warstrider would respond to their every move. Now that I think about it, it didn't actually <i>do</i> anything, but I thought it sounded cool at the time...<br /> <br /> So I explained all this to the players when they managed to read the schematics, &quot;And then you put one of your extremities inside the port, close your eyes and the Warstrider will magically transfer all of the outside stimulus to your characters mind.&quot;<br /> <br /> One of my players looks at me and says, &quot;An extremity? You mean I gotta like, put my penis in there?&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, everyone at the table busts up laughing and I throw up my hands, &quot;No you asshole, one of your <i>hands!</i>. HANDS!&quot;<br /> <br /> But the damage was done. Forever after everyone referred to it as the Cockstrider with a built in penis-port.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must have this Cockstrider. lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11910-wick-black","name":"Wick Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T03:01:13-07:00","id":924831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=924740#post924740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Building on this: I imagine that if you don't get trained by someone else who knows how to pilot that one particular warstrider, there's a lot of trial and error involved. And if you know how to pilot a melef-type interface suit Strider, then when you get into one where you kneel in a circle and meditate to project your awareness in... It'll be a penalty until you can overcome the unfamiliar layout.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bEhh; I prefer the idea that actually being in the warstrider is fairly intuitive and user-friendly by design, with just needing a bit of experience akin to learning to walk again. Certainly I don't really care for the idea of warstriders with buttons or levers at all. Even the image of opening the thing up to depart, I prefer as looking like using the arms to actually unlatch the front or remove the top, rather than something pneumatic.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T06:02:56-07:00","id":924853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=924762#post924762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I consider it to be far too readily abused.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I think it is important to realize how something might be abused or misused, I also think that it is important not to focus so much on trying to curb potential abuse that other aims are given less focus as a result.<br /> <br /> So a game's rules would be better served by focusing on what happens if they are used as intended, and pointing out potential abuses or misuses to ensure they aren't done by accident, than they would be by focusing on trying not to be harder for someone to abuse or misuse, in my opinion. Especially in cases where trying to make the rules harder to abuse makes them less engaging to people not interested in abusing them - because nothing has quite the same degree of disappointment as knowing the reason something isn't as cool as I want it to be is because some other person might do something stupid with it (though I've noticed that the only example I can come up with right now that illustrates what I am talking about is an analogy about the medication that helps me through sinus infections, and how I have to drag myself to the drugstore multiple times while feeling awful and having my ability to drive safely impaired because the rules regarding purchase of medication are written not for me, but for those that want to misuse and abuse them - despite that the effect of the rules is not actually reducing misuse or abuse in any meaningful way).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T10:28:55-07:00","id":924932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=924831#post924831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bEhh; I prefer the idea that actually being in the warstrider is fairly intuitive and user-friendly by design, with just needing a bit of experience akin to learning to walk again. Certainly I don't really care for the idea of warstriders with buttons or levers at all. Even the image of opening the thing up to depart, I prefer as looking like using the arms to actually unlatch the front or remove the top, rather than something pneumatic.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's the great thing, though. You can both be right.<br /> <br /> There could be Warstriders with pneumatic systems, Warstriders that just look like a clay giant with a cavity inside for you to meditate, or Warstriders that are entirely organic and operate by covering you in a silk cocoon.<br /> <br /> I agree with you that it should be fairly intuitive. I see it as being the vehicle itself teaching you how to use it, as you hook yourself up to it, though everyone is free to make up their own reasons (maybe the controls are just that easy to understand; maybe there are no controls, and the entire thing runs on emotional impulses, or telepathy). I like my idea, and yours, and I think Exalted's magic system has enough room that all of the above could be true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11910-wick-black","name":"Wick Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T12:26:42-07:00","id":924980,"title":"","content":"I don't know if anyone posted this but here my two cents!<br /> <br /> I want mundane striders for armor (10-14ft tall) made from gears and pullies. we can call them Battlestriders and have some artifacts too.<br /> I want Warstriders to be larger 15+ feet tall. These can take the role of Mecha and are made for exalted to battle larger enemies. <br /> <br /> I love the idea of large armors and mecha size one's too but I don't want to see a full legion of them. IMO no more than a fang per military.<br /> <br /> There would be a need to have crafter have skill just for them such as craft (striders) and universal charms for them that anyone can take not just solar or dragon blooded. <br /> Also I would like to see universal charms for using the striders themselves. <br /> Overall i would like strider of all type to have a function and stay within that function. Warbirds fly so Battle and Warstriders don't need too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T13:38:49-07:00","id":925017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=924762#post924762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you think Warstriders in your game ought to have Ties and Principles that the pilots must satisfy, that's fine. But I still oppose it being made the official default because, as by now I hope I've made clear, I consider it to be far too readily abused. Solar PCs? All the Warstriders have Tie: Dragon-Blooded. They'll never serve the PCs. These were literally my first thoughts. That to me is an extremely clear indicator of a bad default rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will repeat that I think it should be an option when the strider is designed. I think it should also grant a bonus like the strength of the intimacy added to the evocation dice pools, but also be treated as a Flaw.<br /> <br /> I think Striders that impose them should not get this but instead for this draw back maybe gain another perk like being Dynastic Artifacts.<br /> <br /> I think it should be one of many options each flavorful and evoking a different flavor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T16:54:11-07:00","id":925104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=924762#post924762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That to me is an extremely clear indicator of a bad default rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>With all due respect, if a ST sees a rule and his immediate reaction is &quot;Oh ho ho ho, I can use this to screw over EVERYBODY&quot; I don't think that's the fault of the rules. A ST with that mindset is going to use that mindset with <i>every</i> rule they see. If they don't see an avenue for &quot;I'll make all my Warstriders hate Solars&quot;, they'll see an avenue for &quot;Well this Warstrider only responds to the royal family of Whocares-topia, which you are NOT a member of, so it kills those who would steal it&quot;, or something similar.<br /> <br /> I mean, yeah, we don't want rules that deliberately screw the players, but a jackass ST is going to be a jackass ST. You might as well get rid of artifacts because a ST might destroy them, or get rid of the Wyld Hunt because a ST will say &quot;Okay, after you finish your first meeting... There's the Wyld Hunt, you're facing five monks of each Aspect&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 07-02-2016, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T17:45:06-07:00","id":925132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wick Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=924932#post924932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the great thing, though. You can both be right.<br /> <br /> There could be Warstriders with pneumatic systems, Warstriders that just look like a clay giant with a cavity inside for you to meditate, or Warstriders that are entirely organic and operate by covering you in a silk cocoon.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bI feel as though the presentation of things like this benefit more from a measure of consistency and strongly conveyed aesthetic rather than being something that just any skin could be placed over. That's not a matter of how people play it, they can do whatever they want; I just feel it's a better way to write a book. I think something that tries to be satisfying to everybody ultimately just winds up as lukewarm.<br /> <br /> I would prefer it if the books presented an image other than my own than for it to try presenting every image.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T18:23:33-07:00","id":925150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=925132#post925132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI feel as though the presentation of things like this benefit more from a measure of consistency and strongly conveyed aesthetic rather than being something that just any skin could be placed over. That's not a matter of how people play it, they can do whatever they want; I just feel it's a better way to write a book. I think something that tries to be satisfying to everybody ultimately just winds up as lukewarm.<br /> <br /> I would prefer it if the books presented an image other than my own than for it to try presenting every image.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There only needs to be consistency in the rules. As long as that is true, the window dressing can be anything.<br /> <br /> But we can agree to disagree.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11910-wick-black","name":"Wick Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T18:40:17-07:00","id":925156,"title":"","content":"The presentation of warstriders is much like Lunar shapeshifting - to have coherence, it can't just gobble up absolutely everything without even judging to see if it's appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T19:47:08-07:00","id":925174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=925156#post925156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The presentation of warstriders is much like Lunar shapeshifting - to have coherence, it can't just gobble up absolutely everything without even judging to see if it's appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree but now I want a Chimera that doubles as a warstrider...<br /> <br /> The earlier discussion on Escaflowne makes me wish we had more First Age Weapons. To be clear I dont mean artifact weapons just design philosophies. Like giant blades like the old man's or in Claymore that are designed specifically for penetrating incredibly thick hides/armour back when DB brotherhoods led battalions of Tiger Warriors to bring down giants at the behest of their Solar lieges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","user":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","date":". 07-02-2016, 10:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T00:31:23-07:00","id":925250,"title":"","content":"Regarding Organic Warstriders as a possible variation: Behemoth-summoning Charms or Spells, adjacent to the Warstrider system, would be extra useful.<br /> <br /> Of course, there are a couple of Third Circle Demons that could make that happen for cheap if they'd ever give them the word count.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T01:32:32-07:00","id":925267,"title":"","content":"Late to the general hashing out of ideas (this thread has moved further on to more specific details), for Exalted, that I think would work, at the moment I like my fantasy mecha in about rough two flavours, which I will describe in a sort of stream-of-consciousness style:<br /> <br /> 1) Magitek armour style: Distinctively Second Age creations, with somewhat ramshackle styling that often reveals weak points, larger in scale than a human but not taller than a two storey house. The pilot is somewhat exposed within the armour and, you get a sense like a man riding a war elephant. Sorcerous workings at the armour allow it to summon down magical storms and targeted energy. It moves quickly in forward momentum, and in striking forward, but it is very slow in turning, and can be outmaneuvered by an Exalt on foot in close quarters. The outer armour is fairly light, to reduce weight, and the effect is that a strong Exalted using an weapon artefact and striking at an opportune time (with lots of initiative) can shear through. Beneath the armour, there may or may not be things that resemble circuitry or wires, but there certainly are things that are obliquely related to how the armour moves that pump and flow with fluids and are under tension, and so resemble veins or muscles around bone, and which can be cut through once the outer shell is, sharply reducing mobility and maneuverability for the armour again (leading to a death spiral of mobility).<br /> <br /> (The image is sort of driven by Final Fantasy 6 and Hawkmoon, but not necessarily quite so outwardly steampunk as that, if that's not desired, and by the idea of mighty human warriors fighting war elephants and man sized giants without being overshadowed by them, with a more technological cast).<br /> <br /> 2) Nausicaa style robot agents of the ancient &quot;End Times&quot;: Along the lines of the start of this - <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7wSba9hwCaU\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7wSba9hwCaU</a>. Form a narrative role along the lines of the Thousand Forged Dragons and First Age battleships. Vastly tall, impregnable from without without a similarly powerful weapon (the only hope for human scale warriors is really to enter and destroy from within). Implaceable, faceless and imposing. Depicted in ancient murals as fearsome giants with an odd aspect to them. Armed with genuinely serious apocalyptic destruction (rather than happy explosions!). Terrifying to Creation's enemies. Strictly First Age for the genuine articles - the Second Age has similar facsimiles but they are dependent on scavenged parts, fragile sorcerous works, and break down very quickly into operation, much more vulnerable to attack, and only looks similar rather than posing the same kind of extreme threat. Like every huge multi-storey movie monster ever, they'll turn their attention to you slowly if you're a small scale threat (rationale: they don't give their pilots terribly good tools to detect small scale threats and psychologically, pilots aren't attuned to such threats), then if you fall within their attention, can move towards you with disturbing and frightening alacrity.<br /> <br /> (Dragon Armour a la Escaflowne overlap mostly with style 2), I think, at least as they are in Vision of Escaflowne which is the only Escaflowne thing I've ever seen).<br /> <br /> These are kind of my broad archetypes and imagery in terms of what I want it seems like they should do and feel like - functionally similar but aesthetically varying stuff can work, or things with slightly different tradeoffs (more maneuverable, but weaker in other ways, more sorcerously loaded, etc.).<br /> <br /> Armour in a mid range between these extremes feels like it would end up being be too dominant; too good that an Exalted wouldn't want to go without using it, or if they did, only for reasons of not being able to, technologically, which feels like kind of a buzz kill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T18:47:04-07:00","id":925625,"title":"","content":"I'd like to be able to reenact Xenogears. That game is pretty well defined by its use of mecha and though there are hand-to-hand battles between characters, they don't really mix with the mecha fights. If Warstriders in Exalted can do the things that Gears can do in Xenogears, I'll be satisfied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T01:35:19-07:00","id":925789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=925625#post925625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That game is pretty well defined by its use of mecha and though there are hand-to-hand battles between characters, they don't really mix with the mecha fights.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat's a bit of an awkward translation to a game with superhuman Brawlers, isn't it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmeththeSeventh</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Warstriders in Exalted can do the things that Gears can do in Xenogears, I'll be satisfied.</div> </div> </div> </div> What kinds of things are those?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T02:46:50-07:00","id":925809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Le