all in the &quot;Warstrider / not-quite-an-Artifact&quot; scale?<br /> <br /> Most of them are defeated by a single hero on foot, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say Sahelanthropus is the closest to Warstrider but most fall pretty short of a warstrider or even the Super Robot trope in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T10:50:45-07:00","id":929828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=929824#post929824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say Sahelanthropus is the closest to Warstrider but most fall pretty short of a warstrider or even the Super Robot trope in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about the semi-final boss of Revengeance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T17:23:09-07:00","id":930044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=929828#post929828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about the semi-final boss of Revengeance?</div> </div> </div> </div>Excelcius wasnt even really an MG it was mostly given the label as an ingame marketing ploy. It is actually pretty damned weak given that it is fairly glacial and relies heavily on deploying drones to distract foes. Warstriders are the fear that devours the men who witness a blessed giant descend upon the battlefield wielding weapons that seem like a sick exageration of mortal arms and channeling the incomprehensible power of the god-slaying superweapon within.<br /> <br /> Excelsius is a glorified giant spider in comparison. It has more in common with a really unimpressive behemoth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T01:22:48-07:00","id":930238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=930044#post930044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Excelsius wasnt even really an MG it was mostly given the label as an ingame marketing ploy. It is actually pretty damned weak given that it is fairly glacial and relies heavily on deploying drones to distract foes. Warstriders are the fear that devours the men who witness a blessed giant descend upon the battlefield wielding weapons that seem like a sick exaggeration of mortal arms and channelling the incomprehensible power of the god-slaying superweapon within.<br /> <br /> Excelsius is a glorified giant spider in comparison. It has more in common with a really unimpressive behemoth.</div> </div> </div> </div>You only say that because we see it from the perspective of the guy that beat it. From the perspective of a mighty army of loyal and stalwart soldiers, whose lives are ended by slashing beam swords and great bursts of celestial light, it looks a lot more impressive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T09:52:55-07:00","id":930389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=930238#post930238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You only say that because we see it from the perspective of the guy that beat it. From the perspective of a mighty army of loyal and stalwart soldiers, whose lives are ended by slashing beam swords and great bursts of celestial light, it looks a lot more impressive.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is that Warstriders are usually MEANT to fight things that would find Excelsus unimpressive (vast armies of Demons, Behemoths, other warstriders, etc). Excelsus is meant to LOOK intimidating (it is designed to be big and scary to minimize civi casualties by making them flee) and to bulldoze through urban environments to deal with Guerrillas. Its blades are meant for that I would wager because they seem to slow to be useful against the incredible speed we see from other MGs.<br /> <br /> Sahelanthropus has more of the 'awe' factor and insane mobility of a warstrider (not to mention supernatural aid) while something like REX (by coincidence) and RAY (by design) are able to fight very well with similarly sized foes.<br /> <br /> You also have to consider that most warstriders were built during an age where Tiger Warriors were fairly common in all their inhuman glory so they would have needed considerable agility on their side to hit anything.<br /> <br /> Also a lesser behemoth with diamond sword-arms that can refract light as doom-beams would be plenty intimidating to any conventional army.<br /> <br /> But this ultimately a case of YMMV until we know more, however it is worth noting that the writers seem to be against the Real Robot Trope that MGs are focused on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","user":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","date":". 07-12-2016, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T14:56:28-07:00","id":930536,"title":"","content":"Which makes me sad. I really can't get into the silly magical robots &quot;thing&quot;. I'm suffering through Gurren Lagann, but it brings me no joy. I think my desires for warstriders are out of kilter with the intenitons fo the game, and i'll just have to make my peace with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T04:43:01-07:00","id":1216044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic;n921819[*</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Less parity in the availability of Warstriders, e.g.: certain factions and Exalts generally have no business piloting Warstriders (Lunars, Liminals, Infernals, Exigents, Sidereals), due either to a reasonable lack of necessary infrastructure (Liminals, Exigents) or access to comparable, but fundamentally different magics (Lunars, Inferals, Sidereals), not to say that they couldn't, given access, but what's available isn't designed for them, in so far as most of the readily (relative term) available Warstriders are going to be First Age relics or Shogunate/Realm attempts to duplicate those relics.[/LIST]</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars had warstriders built specifically for them by the Solars of the First Age. These warstriders are unique in that they can shape-shift (albeit in a somewhat limited fashion). Why any Lunar would abandon such wonders in favor of roaming about in the Wyld eludes me.<br /> <br /> But I feel that it would be better if a Second Age Twilight could modify the the original design concepts to fit the current age. For example, if any warstrider unknown to the Realm shows up in the presence of a Realm agent, this would bring the Realm's armies out in force. But, if a Solar can develop a new system or ability, this may be avoidable if the idea actually is feasible. Thus there should be rules to allow for new developments in warstrider technology. Also having the sizes fixed as they are doesn't sound very Solar-like to me. Warstriders of the first age were mass produced and generic for the Terrestrials, but Solar and Lunar warstriders were custom made. The variety of sizes should reflect this.<br /> <br /> As for transforming warstriders; this is not Robotech or Voltron! I can see Lunar warstriders taking on beast forms because it reflects the nature of Luna's Chosen. But this concept doesn't work for Solar warstriders. However, doing as my 2nd Ed Twilight Caste character Sunfire Forge has done (incorporate the folding ship concept into her warstrider so it folds into a backpack) fits a Solar nicely. FYI: the warstrider in backpack form has no room for storage, so I created an artifact that opens a portal to Elsewhere to allow the illusion of storage capacity, and attached the artifact to the 'strider under the backpack flap. I incorporated another artifact into the 'strider to make it light enough to carry in backpack mode. Further while worn as a backpack, the pilot is already strapped in, yet the time to unfold the warstrider into the armor form takes 1 full turn. She learned warstrider construction by cleverly using a cover story to gain access to various libraries with texts on the subject.<br /> <br /> Besides, First Age Twilights were at the cutting edge of Crafts. Solar warstriders should reflect this factor better. Solar warstiders should have the capacity for better traits.<br /> <br /> Lastly, invoking The Great Maker is a way for Second Age Solars to obtain a Second Age AI. After all, Autochthon is a primordial for cryin' out loud. He should have the ability to provide the AI... though the Solar may have to collect a few things first (a soul from the Well of Souls, perhaps? And a vessel to carry the soul in, made by the very Craftsperson that wants to build a warstrider?), then find a way to get these things to Autochthon in Elsewhere. With Autochthon knowing the truth behind the Solar's downfall, I would think The Great Maker would do this as a way of atoning for his silence on the matter... though the Solar asking this of him need not know why Autochthon is so willing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;With the Dragon Blooded attempting to strip us of our place in creation, there are more important things than my life!&quot;<br /> -The last words of Sunfire Forge, Twilight of the Circle of the Forrest's Shade at Dawn","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6919-lady-drager","name":"Lady Drager","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T04:54:15-07:00","id":1216048,"title":"","content":"You necromanced a thread that was dead for two years, man. <br /> <br /> And besides, yes, warstriders that can shapeshift are a handy tool for Lunars, but they require almost constant maintenance, which in turn requires tools, skilled assistants, and infrastructure, all of which makes traveling around harder. <br /> <br /> It'd be like bringing a car with you to the time of the Han Dynasty; sure, it <i>could</i> prove useful, but half of your time is going to be taking actions to keep it in good working order, which in turn presents a massive vulnerability if the predominant empire names you an enemy of the people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-08-2018, 02:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T05:05:40-07:00","id":1216052,"title":"","content":"Also replying to a person that hasn't posted in six months.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lady Drager</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/921517-what-do-you-want-from-warstriders-in-3ed?p=1216044#post1216044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But I feel that it would be better if a Second Age Twilight could modify the the original design concepts to fit the current age. For example, if any warstrider unknown to the Realm shows up in the presence of a Realm agent, this would bring the Realm's armies out in force. But, if a Solar can develop a new system or ability, this may be avoidable if the idea actually is feasible. Thus there should be rules to allow for new developments in warstrider technology. Also having the sizes fixed as they are doesn't sound very Solar-like to me. Warstriders of the first age were mass produced and generic for the Terrestrials, but Solar and Lunar warstriders were custom made. The variety of sizes should reflect this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Luke Skywalker in The Last Jedi quote.<br /> <br /> \u200bThere are no rules for developing new technologies, because that's excessively finickity and largely irrelevant.<br /> <br /> No warstriders are mass produced; like all Artifacts, they're unique and capable of significant power even in the hands of the Terrestrial Exalted.<br /> <br /> \u200bThere might be some variety in warstrider sizes, but the basic concept is predicated on them being large, and somewhat unwieldy. Among other things, it counterbalances their enormous power a bit. Even if one was to downscale the Evocations to something of a size that can more readily do things like enter buildings, one is likely leaning more closely to regular Artifact armour, or possibly some form of First Age Artifice armour.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lady Drager</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But this concept doesn't work for Solar warstriders.</div> </div> </div> </div>All warstriders are Solar warstriders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T05:16:35-07:00","id":1216054,"title":"","content":"There <i>are</i> rules for new developments in Warstrider technology. It's called &quot;Building a Warstrider&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T05:51:04-07:00","id":1216060,"title":"","content":"Don't be cute Lemon, you're too old for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","valu